\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real drags Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  after wider rate cut\b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2023\par 16:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par         * \par       Brazil cuts rate by 50 bps\par     \par \par         * \par       Colombia's cuts 2023 forecasts for inflation, growth\par     \par \par         * \par       Czech Republic keeps rates steady, ends \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par   \par     By Ankika Biswas\par        Aug 3 (Reuters) - A slide in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real dragged the\par Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  index to a three-week low on Thursday,\par as a wider-than-expected interest rate cut took traders by\par surprise, while the Czech Republic's crown touched its lowest\par level this year following a policy decision.\par     The MSCI index for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dropped\par 1.6%, with the real shedding 1.7% and touching\par 4.89-per-dollar intraday, a three-week low.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kicked off its rate-easing cycle with\par a 50-basis-point cut, signaling more of the same going ahead due\par to an improving inflation outlook.\par     The country's interest rate futures also fell across the\par board.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst \f28 \uc2 \f2 Esther Reichelt\f28 \uc2 \f2 , however, believes\par a policy re-evaluation may be under way if the disinflationary\par process in Brazil isn't as fast as expected.\par     Despite the 50-bps cut, Brazil still has one of the most\par attractive real interest rates, which should continue to lend\par support to the real, Reichelt added.\par     As this follows the latest policy easing in Chile and\par Hungary, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's macro strategist Sameer Goel expects\par the rest of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Central and eastern Europe to join in by\par the fourth quarter, followed by parts of Asia and other EMs in\par the firs t half of 2024.\par     Meanwhile, the Mexican peso remained under pressure,\par falling for the fourth day and already losing 4% this week,\par touching a near two-month low of 17.43 per dollar during the\par day.\par     Juan Perez, director of trading at Monex USA, believes the\par peso could cool down slightly, but its economic momentum merits\par the appreciation it has held for the year.\par     "Mexico has come out of the pandemic world far better off\par than most other nations and is enjoying a very fruitful\par relationship in terms of trade with the U.S."\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Colombia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday lowered its 2023\par inflation outlook to 9% from 9.5%, and cut its growth forecast\par to 0.9%. The peso was down 1.6%.\par     Among other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Chile's peso and Peru's sol\par  also lost 0.9% and 1.3%, respectively.\par     Elsewhere, the crown lost over 1% to 24.26 against\par the euro, before paring some losses, after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech Republic's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept rates unchanged as expected and formally ended\par an exchange rate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime to support the crown\par .    \par     "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 CNB\f28 \uc2 \f2  is trying to ease the pressure on the crown by\par announcing the resumption of the program of selling proceeds\par from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves," ING's EMEA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  & Fixed Income Strategist\par Frantisek Taborsky noted.\par     "This time it may be more given that the board has long\par criticized the size of the balance sheet as a legacy of the\par previous board."\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1414 GMT:\par  \par           Stock indexes                   Latest     Daily %\par                                                      change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets                     1015.24      -0.47\par  MSCI LatAm                                2445.34      -1.53\par  Brazil Bovespa                          121309.00       0.37\par  Mexico IPC                               53300.33       0.03\par  Chile IPSA                                6331.33      -0.01\par  Argentina MerVal                             0.00          0\par  Colombia COLCAP                           1173.23       1.06\par                                                              \par              \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                    Latest     Daily %\par                                                      change\par  Brazil real                                4.8893      -1.74\par  Mexico peso                               17.3628      -2.04\par  Chile peso                                  856.5      -0.89\par  Colombia peso                              4129.4      -1.62\par  Peru sol                                   3.6808      -1.29\par  Argentina peso (interbank)               278.3500      -0.34\par                                                     \par  Argentina peso (parallel)                     555       0.90\par                                                     \par  \par  (Reporting by Ankika Biswas in Bengaluru; editing by Jonathan\par Oatis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: