ent risks. Brazil cautions you that a number of factors could cause actual results to differ materially from those contained in any forward-looking statements. These factors include, but are not limited to:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 External factors, such as:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 the impact of the international economic environment on the Brazilian economy, including liquidity in the international financing markets and volatility in international equity, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets; \u8226\'20\'22 the duration and severity of the coronavirus ("COVID-19") outbreak and its impact on the global economy; \u8226\'20\'22 interest rates in financial markets outside Brazil; \u8226\'20\'22 the impact of changes in the credit rating of Brazil; \u8226\'20\'22 the impact of changes in the international prices of commodities; \u8226\'20\'22 economic conditions in Brazil's major export markets; and \u8226\'20\'22 the decisions of international financial institutions regarding the terms of their financial arrangements with Brazil or mature market economies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Internal factors, such as:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 general economic and business conditions in Brazil; \u8226\'20\'22 present and future exchange rates of the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; \u8226\'20\'22 foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves; \u8226\'20\'22 the level of domestic debt; \u8226\'20\'22 domestic inflation; \u8226\'20\'22\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 impact of measures taken to respond to global or national health concerns\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -1-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Table of Contents\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 including contagious disease, such as the ongoing COVID-19 outbreak on the Brazilian economy and Brazil's finances;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8226\'20\'22 the ability of Brazil to effect key economic, fiscal and 