urce: National Treasury\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following table sets forth the expenditures of the Federal Government by function for 2019 through 2022 and the budgeted amounts for 2023. The figures in the table below are not directly comparable to those set forth in Table No. 2 above, entitled "Primary Balance of the Central Government", given that the expenditures set forth in Table No. 2 were calculated in accordance with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  ("IMF") methodology, which does not include, among other things, debt service expenditures and certain financial investments (which, in turn, are accounted for in the numbers set forth in Table No. 3 below).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 S-23\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Table of Contents\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Table No. 2\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Expenditures of the National Treasury by Function\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (In Millions of Reais)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                2019                   2020                   2021       2022              2023Budget (1)   \par Legislative                           6,573.1                  6,305.4                  6,428.5                            6,633.8             10,079.3      \par Judiciary                             32,621.9                 31,448.0                 31,549.4                           34,872.3            45,222.9      \par Essential to Justice                  6,426.9                  6,635.8                  6,663.2                            7,091.9             9,438.1       \par Administration and Planning           22,978.8                 22,229.0                 22,503.6                           23,632.6            28,384.6      \par National Defense                      78,465.7                 76,588.4                 78,191.7                           81,277.2            89,501.8      \par Public Security                       8,449.2                  9,872.1                  9,613.5                     