R$ 93.25 billion (0.93% of GDP).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In February 2023, the Brazilian Social Security System registered a deficit of R$ 21.05 billion, 4.70% higher (in real terms) than the deficit registered in February 2022. For the 12-month period ended February 28, 2023, the deficit of the Brazilian Social Security System totaled R$ 269.93 billion (in real terms). At current market prices, the deficit accumulated in the preceding 12-month period ended February 28, 2023, reached R$ 264.10 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PUBLIC DEBT\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Public Debt Indicators\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Public Sector Net Debt\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of February 28, 2023, Public Sector Net Debt was R$5,706.73 billion (56.64% of GDP) compared to R$5,047.57 billion (56.14% of GDP) as of February 28, 2022.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Government Gross Debt\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of February 28, 2023, General Government Gross Debt was R$7,351.86 billion (72.96% of GDP) compared to R$7,001.66 billion (77.87% of GDP) as of February 28, 2022.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Public Debt\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following table presents Brazil's Federal Public Debt profile as of February 28, 2023.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Table No. 5\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Public Debt Profile\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                  Feb/2023                 Feb/2023             Jan/2023            Jan/2023                  Feb/2022               Feb/2022   \par                                                           %                                        %                                                %          \par Federal Public Debt (R$ bn)      R$         5,856.0                    100.0   %              R$   5,768.7                              100.0   %              R$   5,730.3         100.0   % \par Domestic                         R$         5,616.9                    95.9    %              R$   5,534.7                              95.9    %        