\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chilean peso leaps on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  support,  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real slides\b0\par\par\uc2 589 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Dezember 2022\par 21:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par         * \par       Chile c.bank extends \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program to June 2023\par     \par \par         * \par       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's cost of bank loans hits 5-year high, defaults up\par     \par \par         * \par       \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down 1.9%, stocks off 2.2%\par     \par \par   \par  (Updates prices throughout, adds comments)\par     By Bansari Mayur Kamdar and Shreyashi Sanyal\par        Dec 27 (Reuters) - \par     Chile's peso jumped on Tuesday after its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said\par it would extend its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program, while\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real extended declines to a second day against a firmer\par dollar.  \par     The peso gained 1.3% against the dollar after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chile's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  extended its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program to June 2,\par 2023 from a previously announced end date of Jan. 13.\par         Since last year, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chilean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par aggressively raised interest rates to contain inflation, but a \par     recent poll\par      of traders showed it is expected to keep the benchmark\par interest rate at 11.25% at its January meeting, before an easing\par cycle that would take rates to 6.5% within 12 months.\par   \par         Most Latin American economies are in a much more mature\par stage in their tightening cycle, which analysts say could be a\par contributing factor to growth next year, along with an expected\par boost from China as it loosens strict COVID curbs. \par   \par         The MSCI's index for Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  is eyeing gains of nearly 15% this year, while\par its stocks counterpart is set to end the year flat. Broader EM\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tracked yearly declines of 4.5%,\par while stocks dropped over 22%. \par   \par         "China's tame growth seems set to accelerate in 2023 as\par the country undertakes a bumpy reopening, and EM early hikers\par largely avoided sharp contractions despite their aggressive\par hiking campaigns," economists at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  wrote in a note\par to clients. \par   \par     China said it will stop requiring inbound travelers to go\par into quarantine starting from Jan. 8 in a major step towards\par easing curbs on its borders, which have been largely shut since\par 2020. This helped lift prices of copper, which also supported\par Chile's peso.     \par     Brazil's real slid 1.6% by afternoon trading,\par against a rebounding dollar. Mexico's peso and\par Colombia's peso fell. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data showed borrowing costs in bank\par loans in Brazil rose in November to the highest level in more\par than five years, while default ratios continued to grow, under\par the effects of an aggressive monetary tightening cycle to tame\par inflation.\par     Meanwhile, Brazil's sovereign floating rate bond redemptions\par will hit a record high next year, underscoring the fiscal\par challenge facing President-elect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva\f28 \uc2 \f2  as he\par raises the spending ceiling to fund a social welfare package.\par     The real has been the best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par region, up 5.5% so far this year.\par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1946 GMT:\par          Stock indexes                  Latest   Daily %\par                                                  change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets                   958.77     0.24\par  MSCI LatAm                             2127.45    -2.23\par  Brazil Bovespa                       108150.94    -0.54\par  Mexico IPC                            50373.89      0.2\par  Chile IPSA                             5197.25    -0.48\par  Argentina MerVal                     195804.89    1.729\par  Colombia COLCAP                        1251.14     0.29\par                                                         \par              \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                  Latest   Daily %\par                                                  change\par  Brazil real                             5.2908    -1.57\par  Mexico peso                            19.4771    -0.47\par  Chile peso                               867.4     1.10\par  Colombia peso                             4762    -0.73\par  Peru sol                                3.7981     0.15\par  Argentina peso (interbank)            176.0500    -0.16\par                                                  \par  Argentina peso (parallel)                  352    -1.70\par                                                  \par  (Reporting by Bansari Mayur Kamdar and Shreyashi Sanyal in\par Bengaluru\par Editing by Tomasz Janowski and Chizu Nomiyama)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-12-27T21:02:39.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221227eicr01wd5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pi