\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Softer dollar lifts \uc2 Latam \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; S.African rand weighs on EM\b0\par\par\uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2022\par 22:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par         * \par       Chile's economic activity index down 1.2% in October\par     \par \par         * \par       Brazil's economy grows less than expected in Q3 \par     \par \par         * \par       \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \uc2 \f2  stocks up 0.2%, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  add 1.2% \par     \par \par   \par  (Updates prices)\par     By Bansari Mayur Kamdar\par        Dec 1 (Reuters) - Most Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on\par Thursday, aided by weakness in the dollar, while a drop in the\par South African rand amid rising political uncertainty weighed on\par broader emerging markets.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Latin America rose 1.2%,\par outpacing the broader emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  index\par , which added 0.8%. \par     The U.S. dollar index tumbled 1% after comments by\par Federal Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2  that U.S. rate hikes could\par be scaled back "as soon as December" and as an indicator tracked\par by the Fed showed inflation moderating.\par     South Africa's rand dropped 2.3% against the dollar,\par weighing on the EM index.\par     South African President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cyril Ramaphosa\f28 \uc2 \f2 's future hung in the\par balance as his office said he was exploring options after a\par report found evidence he may have committed misconduct over a\par stash of cash stolen from his game farm.\par         "From a markets perspective, we believe that an early\par departure of President Ramaphosa will be perceived negatively by\par financial markets, given uncertainties about policy continuity\par that such an event would naturally bring," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par strategists wrote in a note.\par     "Hence, against the uncertain political background over the\par next few weeks, we believe that markets are likely to remain\par volatile in the near term."\par     In Latin America, the Brazilian real dipped 0.2%,\par after rising for three straight sessions.\par     Brazil's economic growth slowed more than expected in the\par third quarter as higher interest rates affected household\par spending, underscoring challenges facing President-elect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Luiz\par Inacio Lula da Silva\f28 \uc2 \f2  next year.\par     The real has underperformed its regional peers in November,\par ending last month nearly flat compared to the 1% rise in the\par broader \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \uc2 \f2  index on fiscal policy concerns. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market on Thursday, selling $2 billion in the spot market with a\par repurchase agreement, it said in a statement on its website.\par     Lula has also pushed back his first Cabinet announcements to\par next week, two people familiar with the matter said on\par Wednesday, dragging out key appointments that have kept\par financial markets on edge.\par     Mexico's peso rose 0.6%. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data showed\par remittances to Mexico reached a record-high of $5.360 billion in\par October.\par     A survey showed Mexico's factory activity grew for a third\par straight month in November amid sales improvement, job creation.\par         Meanwhile, a Reuters poll showed Colombia's inflation\par could have peaked in November. The peso \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was up\par 1.3%.\par     Chile's peso gained 1.3%. Traders expect Chilean\par interest rate to remain at 11.25% in December even as recession\par looms in the top copper producer, with data showing a drop in\par the IMACEC economic activity index in October from the same\par month last year.\par     Peru's Sol inched 0.1% up against the dollar after\par data showed consumer prices rose more than expected last month. \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2040 GMT:\par      Stock indexes              Latest    Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets            978.61            0.65\par                                           \par  MSCI LatAm                      2236.94            0.17\par                                           \par  Brazil Bovespa                111036.28           -1.29\par  Mexico IPC                     51753.97            0.13\par  Chile IPSA                      5274.68           -0.15\par  Argentina MerVal              170478.89           1.159\par                                           \par  Colombia COLCAP                 1243.07            0.04\par                                           \par                                                         \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2               Latest    Daily % change\par  Brazil real                      5.1947            0.03\par  Mexico peso                     19.1554            0.50\par  Chile peso                        879.1            1.23\par  Colombia peso                   4762.98            1.34\par  Peru sol                         3.8165            1.01\par  Argentina peso (interbank)     167.7200           -0.24\par                                           \par  Argentina peso (parallel)           309            1.62