\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 After Lula's statements that unsettled the markets, the head of \uc2 Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  called for "fiscal balance".\b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The head of \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Roberto Campos Neto\uc2 , on Friday emphatically defended the need for fiscal balance, following statements by President-elect \uc2 Luiz In\u225\'00\'E1cio Lula da Silva\uc2  that made markets nervous.\par \par \uc2 At an event organized by the CFA Society Brazil group, \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said that the country must be attentive to social problems but also to fiscal balance, "otherwise, we will return to a world of uncertainty".\par \par \uc2 Lula, who will take office on January 1, pushed on Thursday for more room and increased social spending without setting long-term fiscal rules or naming his top economic policy makers, triggering a plunge in Brazilian markets.\par \par \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2 , who will head the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  until December 2024, stressed that the positive dynamics seen at the margin for Brazilian inflation should be confirmed and will depend on the definition of the country's fiscal anchor in the future.\par \par \uc2 The negative reaction to Lula's comments is the most recent example of investors giving an immediate and forceful response to the economic proposals of new governments, amid a challenging global context of high inflation, weak growth and little appetite for risk.\par \par \uc2 In Britain, for example, former Prime Minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  resigned after markets rejected her plans for major tax cuts.\par \par \uc2 "I don't know if there was a \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  moment for Brazil (yesterday), but it was a clear demonstration of the markets' sensitivity to the fiscal issue," \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's autonomy would pass "an important test," but he believed in the continuity of that status under the future Lula administration. \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  also emphasized that the governing body's authorities are open to participating in the transitional government.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the benchmark Bovespa stock index rose last week following Lula's election victory, as fears of political volatility in Latin America's largest economy dissipated.\par \par \uc2 But the president-elect's recent comments, in which he has said he intends to prioritize social spending over market concerns, along with a lack of clarity on his key ministerial appointments, have led to a harsh reassessment of his future government.\par \par \uc2 Investors have said they want Lula to restore firm rules for public finances after current President \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 's big outlays during the pandemic and election season.\par \par \uc2 The real and the Bovespa index fell more than 3% and 4%, respectively, on Thursday after Lula's remarks.\par \par \uc2 (With information from Reuters)\par \par \uc2 Bolsonarista fanatics demanded a military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent Lula's inauguration.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vice-president asked to accept the defeat to \uc2 Lula da Silva\uc2 : "There is no point in crying anymore, we lost the game".\par \par \uc2 US Climate Envoy is confident that Lula will take the necessary measures to save the Amazon\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221112eibc004k0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
