\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  slips as dollar perks up; stocks subdued\b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2022\par 21:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates prices)\par     By Devik Jain\par        Oct 19 (Reuters) - Major Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell\par on Wednesday as expectations of steep interest rate hikes by the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  propped up the dollar, while the yuan hit a\par record low amid caution over the delayed release of Chinese GDP\par figures.\par     The Brazilian real led losses, down 0.6%\par after outpacing its regional peers for the past two sessions.\par The MSCI's index of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slipped\par 0.3%.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market on Wednesday, selling $1 billion in the spot market with\par a repurchase agreement.    \par     "This is in line with Banco Central's policy and they do\par this \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on a case-based analysis, more to provide\par liquidity at a determined moment for the market instead of\par aiming to defend any given \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level," said Wilson\par Ferrarezi, economist at TS Lombard.\par     "We had seen some resiliency in the latam \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but\par the overall outlook for more rate hikes in the U.S. will\par translate into continued pressures over those \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     The dollar index rose 0.6%, while the benchmark U.S.\par 10-year Treasury yield climbed to its highest level\par since July 2008 after another round of hawkish comments from Fed\par officials.\par     A drop in copper and iron ore prices weighed on\par resource-heavy \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The copper-linked Chilean peso\par  inched 0.1% lower as the metal extended losses on worries\par about the global economy due to soaring inflation and the\par prospect of more interest rate hikes to tame it.\par \par     The Mexican peso dipped 0.4% as the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said thought must be given to when its rate hiking cycle\par should end.\par     Colombia's peso lost 1.6% and the Peruvian sol\par  slipped 0.2%.\par     Assets in the export-heavy region have been supported this\par year as commodity prices were boosted by Russia's war in\par Ukraine, but Fed tightening has sapped risk sentiment on fears\par it might tip the U.S. economy into a recession.\par     China's offshore yuan hit a record low against the\par dollar as traders nervously awaited delayed economic indicators\par including third-quarter gross domestic product from Beijing and\par more steers on policy from the ruling Communist Party's ongoing\par congress.\par     Dollar strength combined with weakness in a country's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  translates into higher import bills, which accelerates\par inflation. Add to that a hawkish Fed, developing economies have\par been consuming their stockpiles of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves\par this year at a faster pace than in previous bouts of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par weakness. \par     Meanwhile, focus was also on developments around Brazil's\par election. A poll showed on Wednesday Brazilian presidential\par candidate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva\f28 \uc2 \f2 's lead over President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jair\par Bolsonaro\f28 \uc2 \f2  narrowed ahead of a runoff vote set for Oct. 30.\par     Latin American stocks edged 0.1% higher.\par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1935 GMT:\par      Stock indexes             Latest   Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets          864.63           -1.64\par                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                    2190.50            0.06\par                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa              116393.64            0.56\par  Mexico IPC                   46175.42           -0.29\par  Chile IPSA                    5087.55           -0.69\par  Argentina MerVal            136397.71          -0.832\par                                         \par  Colombia COLCAP               1198.06            0.78\par                                         \par                                                       \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              Latest   Daily % change\par  Brazil real                    5.2750           -0.39\par  Mexico peso                   20.1064           -0.39\par  Chile peso                      972.9           -0.05\par  Colombia peso                 4834.13           -1.61\par  Peru sol                       3.9716           -0.22\par  Argentina peso (interbank)   153.1700           -0.22\par                                         \par  Argentina peso (parallel)         288            0.69\par                                         \par  (Reporting by Devik Jain in Bengaluru, Editing by Angus MacSwan\par and John Stonestreet)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-19T20:55:32.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221019eiaj03vfh\par }\pag