\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  slips as dollar perks up; yuan hits record low\b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2022\par 16:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par        Oct 19 (Reuters) - Major Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell\par on Wednesday as hopes of aggressive interest rate hikes by the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  propped up the dollar, while China's yuan hit a\par record low amid caution over the delayed release of GDP figures.\par     The Brazilian real led losses, down 0.2%,\par after outpacing its regional peers for the past two sessions.\par The MSCI's index of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slipped\par 0.1%.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market on Wednesday, selling $1 billion in the spot market with\par a repurchase agreement.    \par     "This is in line with Banco Central's policy that they\par usually \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market or in the spot or futures\par market when they identify some liquidity issues instead of\par aiming to defend any given \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level," said Wilson\par Ferrarezi, economist at TS Lombard.\par     "We had seen some resiliency in the latam \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but\par the overall outlook for more rate hikes in the U.S. will\par translate into continued pressures over those \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     The dollar index rose 0.6%, while the benchmark U.S.\par 10-year Treasury yield climbed to its highest level\par since mid-July 2008 after another round of hawkish comments from\par Fed officials.\par     A drop in copper and iron ore prices also weighed on the\par resource-heavy \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The copper-linked Chilean peso\par  slid 0.4% as the metal extended losses on worries about\par global economy due to soaring inflation and the prospect of more\par interest rate hikes to tame it.\par     The Mexican peso dipped 0.3%, while Colombia's peso\par  lost 0.9% and Peruvian sol slipped 0.3%.\par     Assets in the export-heavy region have been supported this\par year as commodity prices were boosted by Russia's war in\par Ukraine, but the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's aggressive tightening\par measures have sapped risk sentiment on fears it might tip the\par U.S. economy into a recession.\par     China's offshore yuan hit a record low against\par dollar as traders nervously awaited delayed economic indicators,\par including third-quarter gross domestic product, from Beijing and\par more steers on policy from the ruling Communist Party's\par congress.\par     Dollar strength combined with weakness in a country's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  translates into higher import bills, which accelerates\par inflation. Add to that a hawkish Fed, developing economies have\par been consuming their stockpiles of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves\par this year at a faster pace than in previous bouts of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par weakness. \par     Meanwhile, focus was also on developments around Brazil's\par election. A poll showed on Wednesday Brazilian presidential\par candidate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva\f28 \uc2 \f2 's lead over President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jair\par Bolsonaro\f28 \uc2 \f2  narrowed ahead of a runoff vote set for Oct. 30.\par     Latin American stocks edged 0.1% higher.    \par     Shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hoteles City\f28 \uc2 \f2  surged 29.3% as the\par Mexican hotel chain sold five brands to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marriott International\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par for $100 million.\par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1439 GMT:\par       Stock indexes              Latest   Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets            866.40           -1.44\par                                           \par  MSCI LatAm                      2191.58            0.11\par                                           \par  Brazil Bovespa                116175.92            0.37\par  Mexico IPC                     46320.39            0.02\par  Chile IPSA                      5116.03           -0.13\par  Argentina MerVal              137715.33           0.126\par  Colombia COLCAP                 1203.16            1.21\par                                                         \par          \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2               Latest   Daily % change\par  Brazil real                      5.2660           -0.22\par  Mexico peso                     20.1051           -0.39\par  Chile peso                        976.4           -0.41\par  Colombia peso                   4801.13           -0.94\par  Peru sol                         3.9757           -0.32\par  Argentina peso (interbank)     153.1500           -0.21\par                                           \par  Argentina peso (parallel)           288            0.69\par                                           \par  (Reporting by Devik Jain in Bengaluru, Editing by Angus\par MacSwan)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-19T15:54:17.000Z \par \