\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Interest rate jitters, recession worries crush Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2022\par 21:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Eurozone business activity downturn feeds growth fears\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real, Chile peso down more than 2%\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stocks sell-off; Brazil down 2.7%, Argentine shares drop 4.2%\par \par \uc2 (New throughout, updates prices, market activity and comments)\par \par \uc2 By Amruta Khandekar and Susan Mathew\par \par \uc2 Sept 23 (Reuters) - Brazil's real and Chile's peso dropped over 2.5% each on Friday, leading a sell-off across emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors were gripped by fears about a global recession, driving the safe-haven dollar to 22-year highs.\par \par \uc2 Data showed a drop in business activity across the euro zone and Britain feeding fears of a global economic downturn that followed interest rate hikes and hints of more by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and other central banks this week.\par \par \uc2 Risk-off sentiment prompted a sell-off of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling $2 billion in the spot market with a repurchase agreement. The real was on track for its sharpest daily fall in five months.\par \par \uc2 Crude oil and metal prices slid on worries about weaker demand. Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell 1.2% and Colombia's fell 1.7%. Top copper exporter Chile's peso marked its third straight week in the red.\par \par \uc2 "Over the next couple of weeks, long-term investors may hesitate buying into weakness because it doesn't seem like any economic data release or Fed speak will convince markets that a downshift from this aggressive tightening campaign will be happening anytime soon," said \uc2 Edward Moya\uc2 , senior markets analyst, the Americas at Oanda.\par \par \uc2 Latam\b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have fared better than broader emerging market peers as regional central banks started their hiking cycles early and went big, staying ahead of the Fed.\par \par \uc2 Regional assets also benefited from the rise in commodity prices earlier this year. The Brazilian real has seen volatility in the run-up to elections in October, but is still up 6% for the year.\par \par \uc2 "(Brazil's) fiscal revenues have consistently surprised on the upside over the past 12 months," said Elizabeth Johnson, managing director of Brazil research at TS Lombard.\par \par \uc2 "The outlook for 2023 remains much more challenging, largely because of the massive increase in election-related government spending," she warned.\par \par \uc2 Among stocks, Argentina's main index plunged 4.2%, while Colombia's COLCAP lost 3.4%. Brazil and Mexican indexes lost well more than 2% each.\par \par \uc2 After a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavy week, investors will be watching for more decisions next week, including from monetary authorities in Hungary, Mexico and Colombia, with all expected hike rates.\par \par \uc2 In Colombia, analysts are split, with eight of the 17 analysts polled forecasting a 100 basis points hike, taking the key interest rate to 10%, while another eight expect a 150 bps rise. (Reporting by Amruta Khandekar and Susan Mathew; Editing by Andrea Ricci and David Gregorio) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-23T20:32:05.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220923ei9n03bit\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
