\par\par \b \uc2 Lula advisers draft plans for more aggressive Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  policy\b0\par\par\uc2 623 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2022\par 11:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, July 21 (Reuters) - Economic advisers to Brazil's leading presidential candidate are drafting plans for a more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, including more market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tighter regulation of derivatives to curb volatility, senior aides told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Economist Pedro Rossi, who leads the team drafting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy for leftist former president and 2022 front-runner \uc2 Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva\uc2 , criticized the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for what he called a hands-off approach to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which he said had led to volatility. He insisted that Brazil use the exchange rate as "an instrument for development."\par \par \uc2 Those views put Lula's team at odds with the management of Brazil's newly independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose governor \uc2 Roberto Campos Neto\uc2  has a mandate through 2024, creating the potential for sharp fault lines if Lula wins the October vote.\par \par \uc2 Rossi said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now fails to make full use of its exchange rate policy instruments, including \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, to correct periods of excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation.\par \par \uc2 "Of course, (the exchange rate) must conform to conditions. It must adapt to the balance of the Brazilian economy," said Rossi. "But it must correct market failures, dysfunctionality, poor pricing. It makes no sense to have the most volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the system... among the most important \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and not do anything about it," he added.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real has had the highest three-month implied volatility among Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the pandemic began in March 2020, according to Refinitiv data. Its 17% drop against the U.S. dollar in that period trails only Colombia's peso in the region.\par \par \uc2 Rossi also said Lula could embrace more regulatory tools, calling the derivatives market "completely unregulated" compared to the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which makes it dysfunctional at times. He said regulations could push liquidity from derivatives markets into the spot market, removing "excess speculative positions."\par \par \uc2 He noted that Lula's hand-chosen successor, former President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2 , had introduced a tax on short positions in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives in 2011 to avoid sharp appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as major economies loosened monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 The champion of that policy was former Finance Minister Guido Mantega. He coined the term "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars" while serving under Lula and Rousseff and is now part of Rossi's task force on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not have allowed this excessive depreciation," Mantega told Reuters, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide to around 5.5 reais per dollar, from about 4 per dollar in 2018, which he considered a point of equilibrium.\par \par \uc2 However, bringing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  around to a new policy under Lula would be easier said than done. The bank gained formal independence last year with a law giving its governor a mandate straddling presidential terms.\par \par \uc2 Although prominent economists in Lula's Workers Party have decried the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence, the candidate himself insists he can accept the policy and work with \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rossi suggested the president would have the authority to impose a more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy through the National Monetary Council (CMN), \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's highest-ranking economic policy body, currently comprised of the economy minister, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief and a special treasury secretary.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will respond to the CMN. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not autonomous in defining economic policy objectives. It is autonomous in managing the instruments," he said.\par \par \uc2 Still, Mantega warned that "an independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could make a mess if it's poorly run."\par \par \uc2 "The council can mitigate (dysfunction), but cannot resolve it," he said. (Reporting by Marcela Ayres and Bernardo Caram Additional reporting by Jose de Castro Editing by Brad Haynes and Rosalba O'Brien) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-21T10:00:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220721ei7l01exf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
