\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chilean peso climbs for third straight day; Brazil's Bovespa leads \uc2 Latam\uc2  stocks higher\b0\par\par\uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2022\par 22:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Mexican economy likely grew 2.1% in June on year\par     * Chile's peso surges for third straight day\par \par  (Updates prices)\par     By Anisha Sircar and Devik Jain\par     July 19 (Reuters) - The Chilean peso advanced for the third\par straight session against a retreating dollar on Tuesday, while\par Brazil's Bovespa led gains among the region's stock indexes\par boosted by shares of financials and commodity companies.\par     Chile's peso jumped 2.2%, and has gained 13.1% in the\par last three sessions after last week's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par propped up the struggling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real edged 0.4% higher. State-run \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  said it would lower gasoline prices at its refineries\par about 5%, its first price cut since late 2021.\par     The move brings some relief to President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jair Bolsonaro\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who\par is trailing former President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva\f28 \uc2 \f2  in\par opinion polls ahead of the October vote as high consumer prices\par hurt his popularity.\par     The dollar eased from two-decade highs as markets\par pared bets for a 100 basis point hike by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  next week. The safe-haven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has benefited this\par year on growing worries about a global recession. \par     "A (recovery in EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) comes on the back of very\par large falls last week, (but) it's going to be a challenging\par environment over the rest of the year if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  is tightening aggressively," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 William Jackson\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief\par emerging markets economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Capital Economics\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "We've seen big swings in the Brazilian real over the past\par year triggered by perceived political risk, but now, a lot of\par that bad news is priced in, so a Lula government proving to be\par more moderate might help support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     Mexico's peso was down 0.2% after rising as much as\par 0.76%. The country's economy likely grew 2.1% in June from a\par year earlier, but activity is expected to have contracted by\par 0.4% last month from May, estimates from the national statistics\par agency showed.    \par     Inflation in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \uc2 \f2 's second-largest economy in the first\par half of July likely remained at levels not seen since January\par 2001, a Reuters poll showed, raising bets the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Mexico\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par will raise its key rate again at its August meeting following a\par record 75 basis point hike in June.\par     Argentina's peso surpassed the psychological barrier of 300\par pesos per dollar in the black market earlier in the day,\par hitting a record low as both businesses and individuals hold on\par to scarce greenbacks.\par     Resource-rich \f28 \uc2 \f2 Latam\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have come off highs hit\par earlier this year as a commodity boom loses steam on global\par growth and demand fears, while recession fears, rising interest\par rates and inflation have sent stocks in the region tumbling 6.8%\par this year.\par     Stocks rose 0.4%, with Brazil's heavyweight\par Bovespa up 1.25%, boosted by 3.6% gains in lenders \f28 \uc2 \f2 Itau\par Unibanco Holding SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Bradesco\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     Brazil's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Embraer SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  jumped 7.8% after the\par planemaker announced a partnership with \f28 \uc2 \f2 BAE Systems PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par to expand their footprint in the global defense market.\par \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1935 GMT:\par     \par     \par       Stock indexes                Latest    Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets               980.25            -0.02\par                                              \par  MSCI LatAm                         1983.59             0.41\par  Brazil Bovespa                    98123.08             1.25\par  Mexico IPC                        46978.11             0.12\par  Chile IPSA                         5133.37             1.02\par  Argentina MerVal                 106981.86            1.461\par  Colombia COLCAP                    1298.07             1.28\par                                                             \par           \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest    Daily % change\par  Brazil real                         5.4181             0.13\par  Mexico peso                        20.5013            -0.22\par  Chile peso                           925.7             1.86\par  Colombia peso                       4313.2            -0.39\par  Peru sol                            3.8615             0.77\par  Argentina peso (interbank)        129.1400            -0.18\par                                              \par  Argentina peso (parallel)              296            -1.69\par                                              \par  \par     \par  (Reporting by Anisha Sircar and Devik Jain in Bengaluru\par Editing by Alistair Bell and Richard Chang)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-19T21:06:21.000Z \par \par \uc