\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-EMERGING MARKETS-Chilean peso leads Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  higher as dollar takes a breather\b0\par\par\uc2 630 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2022\par 21:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Dollar weakens as Fed rate hike bets ease; Latam \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  0.5%\par     * Chilean Peso extends Friday rally on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cheer\par     * Bolsonaro to share concerns about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  election with\par diplomats\par \par  (Updates prices)\par     By Anisha Sircar and Devik Jain\par     July 18 (Reuters) - Some Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose\par against a retreating dollar on Monday as a flight to safety\par waned on easing bets around the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par aggressive rate tightening campaign, with Chile's peso leading\par the charge with a more than 3% jump.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit its highest level since July 17,\par after Andean country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  agreed last week to a $25\par billion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  due to the strong advance of the greenback.\par     Also supporting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , prices of Chile's top export,\par copper, rebounded on news about government support for the\par China's economy.\par     The dollar, meanwhile, slipped to a one-week low as\par traders pared bets on how aggressively the Fed will hike rates\par this month. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose 0.5% to their\par highest since July 13.\par     Oil exporter Colombia's peso jumped 1.06% as crude\par prices firmed amid gas supply concerns after Russia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  declared force majeure on supplies to Europe, while\par Mexico's peso added 0.4%.\par     "We've gotten to a point where the world is in chaos, and\par the dollar merits strength, but it doesn't need to be exceeding\par any further," said Juan Perez, director of trading at Monex USA.\par     "But until we have something that determines the\par (Russia-Ukraine) war is going to have a ceasefire, or that\par they're in the midst of negotiations, you're not going to have a\par serious comeback for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Perez added.\par     Latam stocks rose 0.4%, paring gains after\par climbing as much 2.5%. Wall Street's main indexes also erased\par gains to trade lower in afternoon trading.\par     Stocks in recent weeks have been roiled by rising inflation\par and interest rates, cooling commodity prices as well as economic\par strains in China adding to supply-side worries.\par     Argentina's peso underperformed to slip 0.5%, while\par Peru's sol was up 0.4%. Peru's economy expanded 2.28% in\par May compared with a year earlier, the government said on Friday.\par That was a lower growth pace compared to the last three months,\par due in part to a drop in key mining production.\par     Meanwhile, Mexico's tech startups may be enjoying a boom,\par but its top stars are unlikely to list on the country\u8217\'20\'19s own\par stock market, the national exchange's chief executive told\par Reuters in an interview last week.\par     Brazil's real was down 0.2% after rising as much 1.1%\par earlier in the session.  \par     Brazilian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jair Bolsonaro\f28 \uc2 \f2  invited foreign diplomats\par to a briefing at his residence to share his concerns about the\par security of the electoral process ahead of October elections in\par which he is trailing in a bid for a second term.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1909 \par GMT:\par     \par      Stock indexes              Latest    Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets            979.52            1.84\par                                           \par  MSCI LatAm                      1961.12            0.51\par                                           \par  Brazil Bovespa                 96727.35            0.18\par  Mexico IPC                     47041.14           -0.07\par  Chile IPSA                      5082.13           -0.19\par  Argentina MerVal              105439.51           1.167\par                                           \par  Colombia COLCAP                 1275.42             0.1\par                                           \par                                                         \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2               Latest    Daily % change\par  Brazil real                      5.4154           -0.20\par  Mexico peso                     20.4481            0.36\par  Chile peso                        942.9            3.03\par  Colombia peso                   4304.07            1.06\par  Peru sol                           3.89            0.07\par  Argentina peso (interbank)     128.8800           -0.50\par                                           \par  Argentina peso (parallel)           286            2.45\par                                           \par  \par \par     \par  (Reporting by Anisha Sircar and Devik Jain in Bengaluru;\par Editing by Paul Simao and Alistair Bell)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-18T20:48:39.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220718ei7i037w9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
