ents) in amount sufficient so that our total \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure, net of tax effects, is consistent with our low-risk exposure strategy. Our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  position on the liability side is composed of various elements, including the issuance of securities in international capital markets, credit from foreign banks used to finance import and export transactions, dollar-linked onlendings from government financial institutions and deposits in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Latin America countries. The proceeds of these financial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  are usually invested in loans and purchase of dollar-linked securities. The information below has been prepared on a consolidated basis, eliminating related-party transactions. Foreign investments, eliminated during the consolidation process, amounted to R$73.6 billion on December 31, 2021, under the gap management policy adopted, as mentioned above. Note that the bank applies either economic hedge or accounting hedge to net foreign investments. 176\par \par \uc2 R$ million As of December 31, 2021 % of amounts Exchange Rate Sensitivity Denominated in Indexed to foreign denominated in and Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Total foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (1) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (1) indexed to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of total (In millions of R$, except percentages) Assets 1,481,363 532,460 55,383 2,069,206 28.4 Cash 7,383 33,709 3,420 44,512 83.4 At Amortized Cost 986,464 351,422 37,896 1,375,782 28.3 Compulsory deposits in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Brazil 104,592 - 104,592-Interbank deposits 17,795 52,147-69,942 74.6 Securities purchased under agreements to resell 159,974 9,744-169,718 5.7 Voluntary investments with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Cent