eria defined by accounting standards. Transactions or sets of transactions with related parties involving amounts higher than R$1.0 million in the period of twelve (12) successive months must be approved by our Related Parties Committee, composed entirely of independent members of our Board of Directors. Additionally, these transactions are reported to the Board of Directors on a quarterly basis. To access our Transactions with Related Parties Policy, approved by the Board of Directors and last updated on June 9, 2020, please see: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.itau.com.br/relacoes-com-investidores"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.itau.com.br/relacoes-com-investidores}}}\uc2  > Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco > Corporate Governance > Regulations and Policies > Policies. CMV Instruction No. 480/09 requires that transactions with related parties meeting the conditions set forth by Attachment 30-XXXIII thereof are to be disclosed in accordance with the terms defined in such rule. The practices adopted by the Issuer comply with the Brazilian Corporate Governance Code's recommendations, thus ensuring that transactions with related parties are at all times carried out in the Company's best interests, with independence and transparency. The main unconsolidated related parties are as follows: \u8226\'20\'22 Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Participa\u231\'00\'E7\u245\'00\'F5es S.A. (IUPAR), Companhia E. Johnston de Participa\u231\'00\'E7\u245\'00\'F5es S.A. (stockholder of IUPAR) and Ita\u250\'00\'FAsa S.A., direct and indirect stockholders of Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Holding S.A. \u8226\'20\'22 Non-financial affiliates, subsidiaries and joint ventures of Ita\u250\'00\'FAsa S.A., notably: Dexco S.A., Copagaz -Distribuidora de G\u225\'00\'E1s S.A. Aegea Saneamento e Participa\u231\'00\'E7\u245\'00\'F5es S.A., \u193\'00\'C1guas do Rio 1 SPE S.A., \u193\'00\'C1guas do Rio 4 SPE S.A., Alpargatas S.A., and XP Inc. (as from October 1, 2021). \u8226\'20\'22 Main investments in associates and joint ventures, the main ones being: Porto Seguro Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Participa\u231\'00\'E7\u245\'00\'F5es S.A., BSF Holding S.A., and XP Inc. (up to May 31, 2021). \u8226\'20\'22 Funda\u231\'00\'E7\u227\'00\'E3o Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco - Previd\u234\'00\'EAncia Complementar - and FUNBEP - Fundo de Pens\u227\'00\'E3o Multipatrocinado, closed private pension companies that run supplementary retirement plans sponsored by Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Holding, set up exclusively for their employees. \u8226\'20\'22 Associa\u231\'00\'E7\u227\'00\'E3o Cubo Coworking Ita\u250\'00\'FA - a partner of Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Holding, which purpose is to encourage and promote: discussions, the development of technologies, alternative and innovative solutions and business models; the production and sharing of resulting technical and scientific knowledge; the attraction and gathering of new information technology talents that may be characterized as startups; research, development and establishment of ecosystems for entrepreneurship and startups. \u8226\'20\'22 Foundations and Institutes maintained by Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Holding's donations and proceedings generated by its assets to accomplish their purposes, as well as to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  and administrative structure: Funda\u231\'00\'E7\u227\'00\'E3o Ita\u250\'00\'FA para Educa\u231\'00\'E7\u227\'00\'E3o e Cultura - promotes education, culture, social assistance, protection and guarantee of rights, as well as strengthening civil society. Instituto Unibanco - supports projects aimed at social assistance, notably education, culture, promotion the integration into labor market and environmental protection, directly and/or additionally through civil society institutions. 306\par \par \uc2 Instituto Unibanco de Cinema - promotes culture in general and the access of low-income population to cinematography, videography and similar productions, for which it supports the main