\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  falls as U.S. inflation optimism fizzles out\b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2021\par 21:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Bolsonaro seen as risk factor for Brazil IPO pipeline\par     * SoftBank renews LatAm bet, to launch $3 bln investment\par fund  \par \par  (Adds comments, bullets, updates prices throughout)\par     By Susan Mathew and Shreyashi Sanyal\par     Sept 14 (Reuters) - Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell on\par Tuesday after tamer-than-expected U.S. inflation data left\par questions about the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's next move, with Brazil's\par real leading declines in the region. \par     The MSCI's index for Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  fell 0.5%, with Brazil's real down 0.6%\par against the dollar.\par     While prospects of further interest rate hikes in Brazil\par lend some support, tensions ahead of elections next year are\par weighing on the real and companies have cited political upheaval\par from far-right President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jair Bolsonaro\f28 \uc2 \f2  as a new risk factor for\par initial public offerings.\par     Last week, pro-Bolsonaro marches took place across the\par country, with the president calling on Supreme Court Justice\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alexandre de Moraes\f28 \uc2 \f2  to step down and said he would no longer\par comply with his rulings. He later sought to smooth over the\par relationship.\par     "In Brazil, the focus will stay on politics and more\par specifically on whether the truce between the president and the\par Supreme Court will be a lasting one," said economists at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market due to seasonal demand for dollars concentrated near the\par end of the year, its chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Roberto Campos Neto\f28 \uc2 \f2  said.\par     Meanwhile, Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 SoftBank Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  renewed its LatAm\par bet, launching a $3 billion fund to invest in technology\par companies in the region.\par     The dollar index, which measures the greenback\par against six major rivals, fell up to 0.4% as data showed\par underlying U.S. consumer prices rose at their slowest pace in\par six months, creating uncertainty about the Fed's stance on\par stimulus tapering.\par     "While the inflation numbers might be the start of some\par 'relief' and positive for high beta/risk \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , we think\par the market will need to get through the Fed meeting first before\par it can break 'free'," strategists at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. \par     Mexico's peso retreated further from four-week highs,\par down 0.2%. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which has largely been on an upward\par trend, has gained 2.5% over the last 12 sessions. \par     Ratings agency Fitch on Monday warned that Mexico's\par weakening governance is raising credit uncertainties, citing\par energy, utilities, infrastructure and financial institutions as\par the most affected.\par     Among stocks, Brazil's \f28 \uc2 \f2 BTG Pactual\f28 \uc2 \f2  jumped almost\par 3% on a report that Singapore's state investor \f28 \uc2 \f2 GIC Pte Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  is\par investing $421 million into the lender's private equity fund\par that controls fiber optic company V.tal. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b 