te Governance > Rules and Policies > Policies > Transactions with Related Parties Policy. Instruction CVM No. 480/2009 requires that transactions with related parties meeting the conditions set forth by Attachment 30-XXXIII of such rule be disclosed in accordance with the terms defined in such rule. The practices adopted by the Issuer comply with the Brazilian Corporate Governance Code's recommendations, thus ensuring that transactions with related parties be always carried out in the Company's best interest, with independence and transparency. The main unconsolidated related parties are as follows: Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Participa\u231\'00\'E7\u245\'00\'F5es S.A. (IUPAR), Companhia E. Johnston de Participa\u231\'00\'E7\u245\'00\'F5es S.A. (stockholder of IUPAR) and Ita\u250\'00\'FAsa S.A., direct and indirect stockholders of Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Holding; Non-financial subsidiaries and joint ventures of ITA\u218\'00\'DASA, especially: Duratex S.A., Copagaz - Distribuidora de G\u225\'00\'E1s S.A. and Alpargatas S.A.; Main investments in associates and joint ventures the main ones being: Porto Seguro Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Participa\u231\'00\'E7\u245\'00\'F5es S.A., BSF Holding S.A., IRB-Brasil Resseguros S.A., and XP Inc.; Funda\u231\'00\'E7\u227\'00\'E3o Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco - Previd\u234\'00\'EAncia Complementar and FUNBEP - Fundo de Pens\u227\'00\'E3o Multipatrocinado, closed-end supplementary pension entities, that administer retirement plans sponsored by Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Holding, created exclusively for employees; Associa\u231\'00\'E7\u227\'00\'E3o Cubo Coworking Ita\u250\'00\'FA - a partner of Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Holding, which purpose is to encourage and promote: discussions, the development of technologies, of alternative and innovative solutions and business models; the production and sharing of the resulting technical and scientific knowledge; the attraction and gathering of new information technology talents that may be characterized as startups; research, development and establishment of ecosystems for entrepreneurship and startups. Foundations and Institutes maintained by Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco Holding's donations and proceedings generated by its assets to accomplish its purposes, as well as to maintain the \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  and administrative structure: Funda\u231\'00\'E7\u227\'00\'E3o Ita\u250\'00\'FA para Educa\u231\'00\'E7\u227\'00\'E3o e Cultura - promotes education, culture, social assistance, rights defense and guarantee, as well as strengthening of civil society. Instituto Ita\u250\'00\'FA Cultural - promotes and spreads Brazilian culture across the country and abroad. 328\par \par \uc2 Instituto Unibanco - supports projects focused on social assistance, particularly education, culture, promotion of integration to labor market, and environmental protection, on a direct and/or supplementary basis, through civil society's institutions. Instituto Unibanco de Cinema - promotes culture in general and provides access of low-income population to cinematography, videography and similar productions, for which it should maintain movie theaters and movie clubs owned or managed by itself, and theaters to screen films, videos, video-laser discs and other related activities, as well as to screen and divulge movies in general, especially those produced in Brazil. Associa\u231\'00\'E7\u227\'00\'E3o Ita\u250\'00\'FA Viver Mais - provides social services for the welfare of beneficiaries, in the way and under conditions established by its internal rules, and according to the funds available. Among others, these services may include the promotion of cultural, educational, sports, entertainment and health care activities. 16.2. Except for transactions carried out between the issuer and companies in which it directly or indirectly holds 100% of the capital stock, inform, with respect to transactions with related parties that, according to accounting standards, sh