 sheet plus net debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company's main capital management objectives are to safeguard its ability to continue as a going concern, optimize returns, allow consistency of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to other stakeholders and to maintain an optimal capital structure reducing financial costs and maximizing the returns. In addition, the Company monitors adequate financial leverage, and to mitigate risks that may affect the availability of capital in Company development. As a result of the IPO, see Note 2, the Company reduced its net debt improving its gearing ratio and adjusting its capital structure aiming to face new capital challenges from COVID-19 and investing in new ventures through acquisitions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-30\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vasta Platform Limited\par Consolidated Financial Statements as of December 31, 2020 and 2019  \par                                                                     \par                                                                     \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                               December 31, 2020               December 31, 2019 \par                                                               \par Net debt (i)                                      970,047             2,141,214   \par                                                                                   \par Total equity                                      4,785,317           3,100,083   \par                                                                                   \par Total capitalization (ii)                         3,815,270           958,869     \par                                                                                   \par Gearing ratio - % - (iii)                         25          %       223         % \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (i) Net debt comprises financial liabilities (note 7) net of cash and equivalents. (ii) Refers to the difference between