x bases of legal entity and amount recognized based on a separate return method for the carve-out \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . 23 Shareholder's Equity\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 23a. Capital reserve - Share-based compensation\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Share-base compensation plan on combined carve-out financial statements from October 11, 2018 to July 31,2020 - note2a)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On September 3, 2018, Cogna Group's stockholders approved a restricted share-based compensation plan, on which may be granted rights to receive a maximum number of restricted shares not exceeding 19,416,233 shares, corresponding to 1.18% of the Cogna Group's total share capital at the Plan's approval date, excluding shares held in treasury on such date. This program should be wholly settled with the delivery of the shares.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cogna Group's obligation to transfer the restricted shares under the Plan, in up to 10 days from the end of the vesting period, is contingent upon the continuing employment relationship of the employee or officer, as appropriate, for a period of three years from the date the respective agreement is signed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-55\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vasta Platform Limited\par Consolidated Financial Statements as of December 31, 2020 and 2019  \par                                                                     \par                                                                     \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The number of outstanding restricted shares as from December 31, 2019 to July 31, 2020 was 159,919 and the grant date fair value was 10.58. Based on the allocation criteria defined in Note 2a, the Company Consolidated Statement of Profit or Loss and Other Comprehensive Income by R$ 686 for the year ended as of December 31, 2020 (R$ 1,372 for the year ended as of December 31, 2019 and R$ 475 for the period from October 11, 2018 to December 31, 2018).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Share-base compensation plan on consolidated financial statements\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On July 23, 2020 the Company approved its new stock option share plan named ('RSU' or 'Restrict Share Units'). The purpose of RSU plan is to enhance the engagement of eligible persons in the creation of value and profitability of the Company by providing such eligible persons with an opportunity to obtain restricted share units and thus provide an increased incentive fo eligible persons to make significant and extraordinary contributions to the long-term performance and growth of the Company. See below the RSU's plans by share units:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vasta Share Units Plans\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vasta Plans                                             December 31, 2019       Employees Shares transferred from Cogna to the Company (c)     Share units grantedJuly            Share units granted inNovember     Share units to be issued and delivered               December 31, 2020 \par Bonus Vasta Plan to Vasta (a)                                               -                                                                                            -                                                                                    142,323           -              (142,323   )       -         \par Bonus Vasta Plan to Cogna (a)                                               -                                                                                            -                                                                                    269,080           -              (269,080   )       -         \par Long term investment - Vasta to Vasta and Cogna (b)                         -                                                                                            29,736                                                                               821,918           80,950         -                  932,604   \par                                                                   