ds                                                              467,227                                                    1,271,519         -               1,738,746   \par Lease Liabilities                                                  7,357                                                      30,379            121,512         159,248     \par Accounts Payable for business combination                          1,878                                                      1,091             8,624           11,593      \par Suppliers                                                          128,728                                                    -                 -               128,728     \par Reverse Factoring                                                  101,186                                                    -                 -               101,186     \par Suppliers - related parties                                        222,090                                                    -                 -               222,090     \par Other liabilities - related parties                                49,244                                                     -                 -               49,244      \par Loans from related parties                                         29,192                                                     -                 -               29,192      \par                                                                    1,006,901                                                  1,302,989         130,137         2,440,027   \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of December 31, 2019, the Business had negative working capital of R$ 326,550 (compared to negative working capital of R$ 236,643 as of December 31, 2018) mainly due to current suppliers and accounts payables with related parties, such as bonds outstanding, suppliers, loans and other liabilities. see note 28a. - Subsequent events.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Capital management\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Business' main capital management objectives are to safeguard its ability to continue as a going concern, optimize returns, allow consistency of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to other stakeholders and to maintain an optimal capital structure reducing financial costs and maximizing the returns.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 No changes were made in the objectives, policies or processes for managing capital during the year as of December 31, 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-95\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vasta Platform (Successor)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Combined Carve-out Financial Statements as of December 31, 2019, 2018\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and for the year ended December 31, 2019 and for the period from October 11 to December 31, 2018\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 b. Sensitivity analysis\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following table presents the sensitivity analysis of potential losses from financial instruments, according to the assessment of relevant market risks made by Management and presented above.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A probable scenario over a 12-month horizon was used, with a projected rate of 5.96% p.a. as per CDI references rates disclosed by B3 S.A (Brazilian stock exchange). Two further scenarios are presented, stressing, respectively, a 25% and 50% deterioration of the projected rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                               Index - % per year                   Balance as Of December 31, 2019     Base scenario                Scenario I     Scenario II \par Financial Assets                                                   101,7% of CDI                                                       42,539                        2,578              3,223              3,868      \par Accounts Payable for Business Combination                          100% of CDI                                                         (10,941      )                (652       )       (815       )       (978       ) \par