\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 There may be relief for Argentina and Latin America: at midnight the US rate was lowered\b0\par\par\uc2 722 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The overnite square, which keeps positions open after the close of stock, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commodity markets and functions as a market to predict what will happen on Monday, brought good news at midnight Argentina. The main one is that US 10-year Treasury bonds were rising in price and, therefore, their rate of return, which had reached 1.64% on Friday and caused Latin American stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall, was in decline and falling to 1.61%.\par \par \uc2 It is this rate that changed all the rules of the game in recent times and caused a capital flight from the region that felt intense, in addition to Argentina, in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid the devaluation of the real and have to raise interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the real suffered a devaluation of 2.15%, the largest since November last year and higher - in a week - than the Argentine government has planned for all of March. For example, the wholesale dollar ended the week with a 51-cent raise to $90.86 against 57 cents from the previous one. But there are details that make us see that the realities are different: Brazil is concerned that its inflation is more than 4% this year and Argentina, because it does not exceed 30%.\par \par \uc2 Vacuum cleaner\par \par \uc2 Latin American bonds and exchanges also went down because the US bond rate above 1.60% turns the US into a dollar vacuum cleaner in emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The New York Stock Exchanges, at midnight, accompanied this move of bond price hikes with hikes of up to 0.55% as was the case with the \uc2 Nasdaq\uc2  of technology stocks. The dow Jones and S&P 500 ups did not exceed 0.40%.\par \par \uc2 The anchorage goes ahead and helped him a week that ended without start because debt bonds after a sharp fall, between Thursday and Friday they recovered a portion of what they lost and the country risk dropped 47 units to 1,603 basic points after reaching a peak of 1,650.\par \par \uc2 Alternative dollars, both in the market involving the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that of traders, where there are no limits, ended the wheel in balance, but bond indentation followed. As is known, central buys the AL30C bond in dollars and resells it in pesos to hold the dollar Stock Exchange or MEP and cash with liquidation.\par \par \uc2 These \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevent him from making heavy daily purchases of dollars in favor of further liquidation of exporters cannot significantly raise reserves.\par \par \uc2 Bonds yes, non-imports\par \par \uc2 On Friday in the wholesale square where $261 million was operated, Central bought $105 million, but reserves grew to just $17 million to $39,823 million. It should be narrowed that these high purchases are achieved by sacrificing demand from importers to whom it delivers dollars in minimum quantities.\par \par \uc2 Developments in foreign markets helped Argentine stocks. The Buenos Aires Stock Exchange ended with a weekly rise of 3.87% by boosting the shares of banks and oil companies.\par \par \uc2 On Friday in the wholesale square where $261 million was operated, Central bought $105 million, but reserves grew by just $17 million\par \par \uc2 In the overnite market, oil was trading 1% up, both in the Brent, which is a benchmark in Europe, and in the WTI which is the U.S. indicator used by Argentina. But this good news for the country, due to the situation of Vaca Muerta and \uc2 YPF\uc2 , becomes a problem because fuel is one of the elements that drives the price hike and that the government intends to keep it regulated and with increases below inflation.\par \par \uc2 With 15 days to go before filing returns and paying the first installment of the callwealth tax, the dollar is in a position that can be controlled, but at a very high cost in terms of reserves. The government's problem is that two days of good bond performance does not guarantee that it will be able to keep the dollar under control, let alone inflation.\par \par \uc2 READ ON:\par \par \uc2 Pandemic effect: Argentina, among the countries that reduced cash use the most, although it remains among the highest\par \par \uc2 Sticks on the wheel producing dollars: stories of suppliers of the field, drowned by import jams\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210315eh3f001sl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
