\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  cenbank announces up to $1 bln  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  swap  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  for Thursday\b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par 00:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, March 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would sell up to $1 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps on Thursday, extending its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with the real hovering near its all-time low against the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The announcement follows two separate \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, one a $1 billion sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and the other a $405 million sale in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The real is one of the worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world this year but rallied more than 2% on Wednesday, its biggest daily gain since late January.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week it had slumped to 5.88 per dollar, close to last year's record low around 5.97 per dollar and taking its year-to-date decline to around 11%.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, this time taking advantage of a rebound in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than attempting to slow its decline, suggests a more aggressive approach.\par \par \uc2 "(This sends) a strong message to anchor financial conditions and causes discomfort to those speculating against the real," said a senior trader in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Strategists at Citi said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action is a key factor behind their near-term bullishness on the real.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent proactive stance with its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... seems to be here to stay in the near term," they wrote in a note, citing increased nervousness over inflation. "This adds another layer of support for the real."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to raise interest rates next week for the first time in five years, which should also lend some support to the real, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold $5.58 billion in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and $6 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps market, according to brokerage Commcor DTVM. (Reporting by Jamie McGeever; Editing by Stephen Coates)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-3-13T23:19:43.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210310eh3a047p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
