\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Brazil real slide not justified by fundamentals,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  president says\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par 00:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Jamie McGeever and Gabriel Ponte\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, March 2 (Reuters) - Brazil's real has suffered more than other emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors adjust to changing liquidity conditions globally, but some of it has not been justified by economic fundamentals, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Roberto Campos Neto\uc2  said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in an online event hosted by Arko Advice and Empiricus, \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has large \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and will continue to act as it sees fit, adding that it remains focused on using all the tools at its disposal to meet it inflation goals.\par \par \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  was speaking on the day the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market selling $2.1 billion as the real hit a three-month low against the dollar, taking its dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last Thursday to over $5 billion.\par \par \uc2 Growing worries over Brazil's fiscal outlook explain part of the real's weakness, while global jitters as markets adjust to the worldwide rise in bond yields have also made it easier for traders to attack the real, he said.\par \par \uc2 "But we believe part of the move is not justified by fundamentals. We have increased our presence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market recently and Brazil has a very large amount of reserves," \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "We can continue acting in ways we believe are reasonable to always maintain conditions of (good) liquidity," he added.\par \par \uc2 The real closed at its lowest level on Tuesday since Nov. 3, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions were its fifth and sixth bouts of direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2 , however, again warned that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  must get its public finances back in order, noting that investors are generally right to increase the risk premium on Brazilian assets if they believe the fiscal fundamentals are deteriorating.\par \par \uc2 "If you have a perception of deteriorating fundamentals allied to a perception that emerging market liquidity is going to fall, then this volatility leads to bigger (price) moves," he said.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 5.67 reais)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jamie McGeever and Gabrioel Ponte Editing by Chris Reese and Lisa Shumaker) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-3-3T00:51:10.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210302eh3203v9x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
