\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Covid-19 and devaluation: "storm" in Brazil that worries the Rosada\b0\par\par\uc2 723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Despite the jump in the February trade surplus, the "explosion" of the coronavirus pandemic in Brazil, coupled with a sharp devaluation,already worries the Government that it does not know what the exchange of goods and services will look like this month, closures of industries and shops included in the neighboring country.\par \par \uc2 Official sources consulted by BAE Negocios referred to growing uncertainty as "the dollar todayalmost touches the 6 reais, a historic high, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 Also, in the health order, no lessthan "17 of the 27 States have 95% of intensive care beds occupied", with restrictionson the opening of factories and shops in some areas.\par \par \uc2 Another element is added to the analysis and is that while two months ago public opinion alluded to growth by the South American giant by 2021,"Brazil's GDP drop today is estimated for the first quarter between 0.4% and 1.3%, the latter calculation since \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 Factor "Covid-19" At least 18 Brazilian capitals find more than 80% of bed occupancy for Covid-19, according to the latest survey by the Fiocruz state laboratory, and 17 of the 27 states own 95% of occupied intensive care beds.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian states of Santa Catarina and Minas Gerais collapsed through the second wave of coronavirus and had to transfer serious patients to other regions of Brazil, officially reported on Tuesday, amid the worst time of the pandemic in the country, aggravated by the spread of the so-called Amazon strain,a more contagious variant.\par \par \uc2 However, Vice President Antinio Hamilton Mour\u225\'00\'E1o on Tuesday set out tougher restrictions at the national level to contain the advance of the virus, as the health authorities are calling for.\par \par \uc2 "Each population has its characteristics;\u160\'00\'A0if you look at the country there are five different countries in one; the north is one thing, the northeast another, etc.. so there's no point in wanting to impose something national," the government's number two defended in press statements, according to local news portal G1.\par \par \uc2 Since the pandemic erupted more than a year ago in the country, Brazil has accumulated 255,720 dead and more than 10.5 million reported cases, that is, it is the second country with the highest fatalities and the third in number of contagions.\par \par \uc2 Strong devaluation \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spoke on Tuesday in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the fifth time in four days, as investors' concerns about the government's fiscal health brought the real close to last year's all-time low of $6 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Tuesday's $1 billion sale, which has lifted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Thursday to more than $4 billion, occurs when pressure on Brazilian assets intensifies after President \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2  eliminated some fuel taxes and increased another to banks," the sources consulted point out.\par \par \uc2 The real has lost 8.5% against the dollar this year. Apart from the Libyan dinar and the Sudanese pound, which suffered huge timely devaluations, it is the world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that behaves the worst against the dollar this year, according to Refinitiv data.\par \par \uc2 "Thereis a crisis of (market) confidence in the government, and we have negative rates," said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a Bank in Sao Paulo, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark interest rate is2.00%, while inflation stands at around 4.5%. The real one was trading at 5,6950 per dollar, its lowest level in three months and about to reach last year's all-time low, just below 6 reais per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Industrial, expectant On the other hand, industrial sources told BAE Business that"bilateral trade can be affected if there is a drop in activity level and an exchange rate devaluation;\u160\'00\'A0you have to wait for the trend and it's going to influence whether it's durable."\par \par \uc2 "While it is difficult to make a forecast, everything indicates that in Argentina there will be exchange rate appreciation, and if Brazil stays on these quotes, Argentina would find it more difficult to export,"they added.\par \par \uc2 "Trade between the two countries is greatly influenced by their growth, by their level of activity. We hope that Brazil will not experience a recessive situation because it will have a negative effect," they said.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210302eh32009l3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
