\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real hits 4-month low on populist policy fears\b0\par\par\uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par 20:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Most Latam stocks gain\par     * Brazilian bank stocks drop after report of higher taxes\par     * Real nonplussed by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par \par  (Adds details, updates prices)\par     By Susan Mathew and Ambar Warrick\par     March 2 (Reuters) - Brazil's real sank to a four-month low\par on Tuesday after government action to curb fuel prices raised\par concerns over a shift to populist policies, while other Latin\par American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remained on edge over high bond yields. \par     The real plunged 1.4% after President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jair\par Bolsonaro\f28 \uc2 \f2  said he would issue a decree on Tuesday suspending a\par tax on diesel fuel, a move aimed at placating truckers who had\par threatened to strike.\par     Sources also told Reuters the government would instead hike\par taxes on banks' net income to about 23% from 20% to offset lost\par revenue.\par     Shares in some of the country's biggest banks, such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Itau\par Unibanco\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bradesco\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Santander\par Brasil\f28 \uc2 \f2 , lost between 0.1% and 1%, while the Bovespa\par stock index was subdued, having touched a more than\par three-month low in the session. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market for the fifth time in four days on Tuesday to\par support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which was last trading at 5.68 per dollar.\par  \par     Fears of populist policy measures have risen since Bolsonaro\par ousted state-run oil company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' chief\par executive in February over disagreements on fuel prices, and\par threatened to interfere in other sectors of the\par economy.\par     "The overall news flow since last week has not be conducive\par for a positive price action in (Brazil) markets," said Latam\par strategists at Citi Research. \par     "Investor optimism will remain suppressed after the\par government's meddling to prevent a rise in fuel prices, and the\par potential dilution of compensatory measures in the emergency\par bill. Thus, we have a negative bias for asset prices in the\par short-term."\par     Brazil's government is considering extending an emergency\par coronavirus aid program amid worries of breaching the\par government's spending cap - an issue that has weighed on\par Brazilian assets.\par     Concerns over a local variant of the coronavirus have also\par undercut Brazilian assets recently, with scientists warning that\par it can re-infect people who have previously recovered from the\par disease.\par     Most other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Latin America fell against a steady\par to higher dollar, in line with broader emerging market peers as\par concerns over spiking bond yields persisted.\par     Chile's peso dropped 0.9%, while Colombia's peso\par  shed 1%. \par     Emerging market stocks and bonds saw foreign net inflows of\par about $31.2 billion in February, though rising U.S. interest\par rates triggered a slowdown during the last week, data from the\par Institute of International Finance showed on Tuesday.\par \par     Still, other Latam stocks recovered from recent losses, with\par equities still being seen as most primed to benefit from an\par economic recovery this year. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par     \par                               Latest       Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets         1362.23                 -0.02\par                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                    2225.75                 -0.46\par                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa              110191.37                 -0.13\par                                         \par  Mexico IPC                   45722.51                  2.09\par                                         \par  Chile IPSA                    4706.93                   1.5\par                                         \par  Argentina MerVal             48144.56                -1.738\par                                         \par  Colombia COLCAP               1350.41                 -0.39\par                                         \par                                                             \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              Latest       Daily % change\par  Brazil real                    5.6817                 -1.42\par                                         \par  Mexico peso                   20.6375                  0.01\par                                         \par  Chile peso                      728.7                 -0.93\par                                         \par  Colombia peso                  3654.5                 -1.00\par  Peru sol                       3.6657                 -0.27\par                                         \par  Argentina peso                90.1500                 -0.07\par  (interbank)                            \par                                         \par  \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew and Aaron Saldanha in Bengaluru;\par Editing by Jane Merriman and Jonathan Oatis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-3-2T20:15:16.000Z \p