\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil markets hit by policy worries after tax changes\b0\par\par\uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par 16:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Susan Mathew\par     March 2 (Reuters) - Brazilian shares touched their lowest\par since November on Tuesday, and the real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a\par four-month trough after action to  prevent a rise in fuel\par prices, raising fears of more government meddling in the\par economy. \par     Brazilian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jair Bolsonaro\f28 \uc2 \f2  said he would issue a\par decree on Tuesday suspending a tax on diesel fuel, a move aimed\par at placating truckers who threatened to strike. Sources told\par Reuters the government would instead hike taxes on banks net\par income to about 23% from 20% to offset lost revenue.\par     Shares in some of the country's biggest banks, such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Itau\par Unibanco\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bradesco\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Santander\par Brasil\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost between 0.1% and 1%. \par     Losses on the Bovespa stock index were broad-based,\par pushing it 1.6% lower, while the real lost more than 1%.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market for the fifth time in four days on Tuesday to\par support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which was last trading at 5.68 per dollar.\par  \par     Meanwhile, Brazilian Economy Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paulo Guedes\f28 \uc2 \f2  said he\par will stay in his post as long as he has the confidence of\par Bolsonaro. \par     Their relationship came under scrutiny since the president\par ousted state-run oil company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' chief\par executive in February over disagreements on fuel prices and\par threatened to interfere in other sectors of the\par economy.\par     "The overall news flow since last week has not be conducive\par for a positive price action in (Brazil) markets," said Latam\par strategists at Citi Research. \par     "Investor optimism will remain suppressed after the\par government's meddling to prevent a rise in fuel prices, and the\par potential dilution of compensatory measures in the emergency\par bill. Thus, we have a negative bias for asset prices in the\par short-term."\par     Brazil's government is considering extending an emergency\par coronavirus aid program amid worries of breaching the\par government's spending cap - an issue that has weighed on\par Brazilian assets.\par     Most other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Latin America fell against a steady\par to higher dollar, in line with broader emerging market peers.\par Mexico's peso swayed in volatile trade and was last at\par 20.645 to the dollar.\par     Emerging market stocks and bonds saw foreign net inflows of\par about $31.2 billion in February, though rising U.S. rates\par triggered a slowdown during the last week, data from the\par Institute of International Finance showed on Tuesday.\par \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1438 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                    Latest     Daily %\par                                              change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets            1361.26    -0.09\par  MSCI LatAm                       2193.00    -1.93\par  Brazil Bovespa                   108530.97  -1.63\par  Mexico IPC                       0.00       0\par  Chile IPSA                       4657.94    0.44\par  Argentina MerVal   