\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  govt  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  threatens privatization, growth prospects -\uc2 Moody's\b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2021\par 23:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Jamie McGeever\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Feb 24 (Reuters) - Brazilian President \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 's decision to replace the head of state-run oil giant \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  threatens the government's privatization program and potentially the economy's medium-term growth prospects, ratings agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2  warned on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The greatest risk to Brazil's sovereign credit profile is a confidence shock that leads to a sharp increase in risk premia. President \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 's action increases political noise and uncertainty over structural reforms this year," \uc2 Moody's\uc2  sovereign analysts team led by Samar Maziad wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 Bolsonaro's shock move after a spat with the outgoing chief executive over fuel price hikes prompted investors to dump Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks, while pushing up interest rates. Some 100 billion reais ($18 bln) was wiped off the value of \uc2 Petroleo Brasileiro SA\uc2  over Friday and Monday.\par \par \uc2 Markets recovered Tuesday and Wednesday, but sentiment remains fragile.\par \par \uc2 "The negative market reaction to this decision sends a clear signal that reversing course on broader reforms could have meaningfully negative implications for fiscal dynamics if interest rates were to increase ahead of the economic recovery or risk premia were to sharply rise," \uc2 Moody's\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Bolsonaro went into damage limitation mode on Tuesday, delivering to Congress a provisional measure associated with his government's plans to privatize state-run electricity provider Eletrobras,.\par \par \uc2 "Our privatization agenda is going full steam ahead," he said.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's economy is likely to shrink in the first quarter due to the second wave of the COVID-19 pandemic and end to government income transfers to the poor at the end of last year, a growing number of economists say.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to raise interest rates sooner rather than later, perhaps as early as next month, against a backdrop of sticky inflation and intensifying worries over the government's fiscal position.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  has a sub-investment grade Ba2 rating on Brazil's sovereign credit, with a stable outlook. (Reporting by Jamie McGeever Editing by Marguerita Choy) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-2-24T23:24:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210224eh2o0569n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw181\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2715\pichgoal600
