\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real jumps, stocks hit record high on upbeat data\b0\par\par\uc2 497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2020\par 20:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Brazil stocks briefly hit record high\par     * Oil-linked \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain\par     * Real bounces of one-month low\par \par  (Adds details, updates prices)\par     By Shashank Nayar and Ambar Warrick\par     Dec 29 (Reuters) - Brazil's real jumped on Tuesday and stock\par markets hit an all-time high as upbeat data and hopes of a\par bigger U.S. stimulus package drove year-end buying into Latin\par American assets set to benefit from a speedy economic recovery.\par     The real bounced off a one-month low to trade\par up 0.9%, as the government reported a November budget deficit\par well below forecasts.\par     Data also showed Brazil's jobless rate fell for the first\par time this year in the three months through October, while a\par survey showed consumer confidence increased in December for the\par first time in three months.\par     Sao Paolo stocks briefly hit a record high, as the\par readings pointed towards improving trends in Latin America's\par largest economy, while investors also expected increased\par liquidity in the United States to benefit regional risk assets.\par \par     "The wider fiscal package from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Congress\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the\par Brazilian economy getting better has helped improve the investor\par outlook towards Brazilian risk assets," said Mauricio Une,\par senior economist at Rabobank.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Monday for the first time in two months after\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slipped to a one-month low against the dollar. \par     But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is still one of the worst performing\par emerging market units this year, given that Brazil is among the\par worst afflicted by the coronavirus.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of oil exporters Mexico and Colombia\par   gained as oil prices rallied on hopes that\par expanding U.S. pandemic aid would spur fuel demand.\par     Hopes of improving oil demand have aided the Mexican and\par Colombian pesos, while Chile's peso is set to outperform\par its Latin American peers for the year, thanks to recovering\par copper demand. \par     Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have recovered\par from pandemic-driven lows. But they have severely underperformed\par their broader emerging market peers over\par concerns about fiscal health and the rampant spread of the virus\par in the continent. \par     Most regional stocks have also followed a similar trend. But\par the MSCI's index of regional stocks rose nearly\par 2% for the day.\par     Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\par     \par                               Latest     Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets         1266.32               1.12\par                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                    2463.50               1.91\par                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa              119480.21                0.3\par                                         \par  Mexico IPC                   44637.92               1.72\par                                         \par  Chile IPSA                    4198.15               0.43\par                                         \par  Argentina MerVal             51538.77               2.09\par                                         \par  Colombia COLCAP               1439.13               0.56\par                                         \par                                                          \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              Latest     Daily % change\par  Brazil real                    5.1903               0.93\par                                         \par  Mexico peso                   19.9370               0.32\par                                         \par  Chile peso                      714.4              -0.35\par                                         \par  Colombia peso                 3472.93               0.67\par  Peru sol                        3.618              -0.03\par                                         \par  Argentina peso                84.0200              -0.13\par  (interbank)                            \par                                         \par  \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Shashank Nayar in Bengaluru; editing by Barbara\par Lewis and Grant McCool)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-12-29T20:28:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201229egct027ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
