\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chilean, Colombian pesos rise; Brazil's real at near 1-mth low\b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2020\par 20:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets\par     * Oil, copper prices benefit Chilean, Colombian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * Latam stocks gain, tracking Wall Street\par     * Argentine assets sink on agriculture export delay\par \par  (Adds market details, updates prices)\par     By Ambar Warrick\par     Dec 28 (Reuters) - Chilean and Colombian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  outpaced\par their Latin American peers in slim trade on Monday, tracking\par higher copper and oil prices as demand prospects improved after\par U.S. President Donald Trump signed a coronavirus relief package.\par     Brazil's real sank as much as 1.8% to a near\par one-month low to the dollar, prompting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to stabilize the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The bank had vowed to support the\par real through the expected year-end unwinding of positions on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The real shrugged off data that showed industrial confidence\par in December rose to its highest level in over a decade.\par \par     Trump late on Sunday signed the $2.3 trillion relief and\par spending bill, which implied positive economic prospects and\par high near-term liquidity in the world's largest economy.\par \par     This in turn fed in to commodity prices, especially copper\par and oil, even as the rapid spread of the coronavirus weighed on\par sentiment. Copper and oil demand is considered to be a\par bellwether of economic outlook.\par     Chile's peso added 0.2% to the dollar. The country is\par the world's largest exporter of copper. Crude exporter\par Colombia's peso rose 0.5%.\par     Other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region retreated, with MSCI's basket\par of Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shedding 0.7%.\par Regional stocks rose, tracking record highs on\par Wall Street.\par     While improving risk appetite and sustained fiscal and\par monetary support have helped Latin American assets rally off\par lows hit due to the pandemic, they are still set to end the year\par lower due to concerns over fiscal health, as well as a second\par wave of coronavirus infections. \par     Mexico's peso dropped after the country's government\par issued new regulations to limit the ability of private companies\par to import fuel, according to a weekend decree, fanning concerns\par that the move may unduly benefit national oil company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleos\par Mexicanos\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Pemex\f28 \uc2 \f2 ).\par     Argentine stocks and the peso tumbled after\par the loading of more than 140 agricultural export ships in\par Argentina was stalled by a port-side oilseed workers' strike.\par Agricultural exports are a crucial source of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par for the country, which has been struggling to restructure its\par sovereign debt for most of this year.\par     Most other global risk assets gained as investors cheered a\par last-minute trade deal signed between Britain and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European\par Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  last week, just seven days before London exits one of the\par world's biggest trading blocs.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\par     \par                               Latest     Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets         1252.48              -0.22\par                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                    2428.29               0.13\par                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa              119098.33                1.1\par                                         \par  Mexico IPC                   43792.57               0.97\par                                         \par  Chile IPSA                    4180.98               1.13\par                                         \par  Argentina MerVal             50566.53             -2.039\par                                         \par  Colombia COLCAP               1426.89               0.33\par                                         \par                                                          \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              Latest     Daily % change\par  Brazil real                    5.2576              -1.00\par                                         \par  Mexico peso                   20.0350              -0.89\par                                         \par  Chile peso                      711.9               0.22\par                                         \par  Colombia peso                 3496.25               0.47\par  Peru sol                        3.617              -0.19\par                                         \par  Argentina peso                83.9000              -0.64\par  (interbank)                            \par                                         \par  \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Ambar Warrick and Shashank Nayar in Bengaluru\par Editing by Jonathan Oatis and Matthew Lewis)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-12-28T20:24:24.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201228egcs027h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley