\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  sells $530 mln in spot  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2020\par 19:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , chart)\par \par \uc2 By Jamie McGeever\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Dec 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday for the first time in two months, selling $530 million after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had slipped to a one-month low against the U.S. dollar .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in typically illiquid year-end trading occurred after the real had fallen below 5.31 per dollar, a slide of more than 2% which had put it on course for its steepest one-day depreciation in three months.\par \par \uc2 The sale helped the real claw back about half of its earlier losses to trade around 5.27 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers had said last month the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the market was unable to absorb outflows related to local banks unwinding their so-called overhedge trades put on to protect their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure on overseas equity investments by Dec. 31 for tax purposes.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director Bruno Serra said on Nov. 18 that this total exposure stood at just under $30 billion, half of which was to be unwound by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 This was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first spot market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Oct. 30, although it has sold dollars in the repo market in the last couple of months.\par \par \uc2 The real has fallen 30% against the dollar this year, making it one of the worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world against the greenback. The main drivers have been Brazilian interest rates being slashed to a record low 2.00% and growing concern about the country's fiscal health.\par \par \uc2 The real made a potentially significant technical upside break a month ago when the dollar fell below its 200-day moving average and slid toward the 5.00 reais level. But that momentum faded, and has now reversed.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jake Spring and Jamie McGeever Editing by Paul Simao) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-12-28T19:51:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201228egcs0268p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
