\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2 : exchange rate is floating and BC  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  when there are liquidity problems\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Roberto Campos Neto\uc2 , reinforced on Thursday, 17, the idea that, for the institution, the exchange rate is fluctuating in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 . According to him, bc makes \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market only when there are liquidity problems.\par \par \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  also pointed out that the flows have "great importance" in the exchange scenario. He recalled that in recent months the country has again received investments focused on portfolio and said that, "apparently, the first weeks of December are also being positive flow to Brazil".\par \par \uc2 In December, the spot dollar accumulates so far low of 5% against the real. In November, amid the influx of foreign resources, there was a drop of 6.83%. \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  also said that the dollar has become weaker against the real, but also against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other countries.\par \par \uc2 Addressing bc's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce the effects of the disassembly of overhedge by banks, he said the issue is "important" for generating atypical flow in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, BC has promoted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions to facilitate disassembly by banks with investments abroad.\par \par \uc2 Overhedge represents the excess hedge that banks with overseas \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  carry and that needs to be reduced by the end of this year. According to some calculations, he totaled $16 billion. By offering swaps, BC seeks to reduce any dollar buying pressures in the futures market by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  also stated that, by the end of the year, new exchange flows may arise, but that the evaluation of how to act is done on a day-to-day and day-to-day.\par \par \uc2 Investors\par \par \uc2 The President of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also assessed that the first investor who returns to the country when confidence improves is the short-term, which invests in portfolio, and not the one that injects resources such as Direct Investments in the country.\par \par \uc2 "When we look at the great crisis of 2008, we see that there was great volatility of IDP. We have a similar behavior of the IDP in the comparison between 2008 and now", he said. "But we are seeing portfolio investor's return, November was a month of strong entry into the Stock Exchange and fixed income," he added during the press conference on the Quarterly Inflation Report (\uc2 RTI\uc2 ) released thursday by BC.\par \par \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  pointed out that the world interest rate remains very low, with programs still ongoing. At the same time, there is an improvement in confidence with the expectation of vaccination. "These three elements will make flows for emerging countries grow a lot. I think the market is anticipating this effect a little bit," he added.\par \par \uc2 The president of bc said that part of the liquidity is returning to Brazil and that to capture more of this liquidity, Brazil needs to have more credibility. "Credibility today is very much associated with the fiscal. I have passed on this message," he concluded.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201217egch0077c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
