\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  eases off gains; Mexico's peso, Brazil's real rise\b0\par\par\uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2020\par 20:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Brazil GDP growth next year could top 4% - economy\par minister\par     * Mexico's peso set to snap two-day losing streak \par     * Regional stocks fall as broader EM retreats\par \par  (Adds details, updates prices)\par     By Shriya Ramakrishnan and Ambar Warrick\par     Nov 19 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso and Brazil's real led gains\par across Latin America on Thursday amid hopes of a swift\par post-pandemic recovery in the region's two largest economies,\par while most other units eased as excitement over a vaccine cooled\par with a surge in global infections.\par     Mexico's peso strengthened 1.1% and was set to snap a\par two-day losing streak, having benefited from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par recently signalling a pause to a rate-cutting cycle.\par     Democratic candidate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Joe Biden\f28 \uc2 \f2 's victory in the U.S.\par presidential election also raised hopes for more stable trade\par policies.\par     Mexico earlier this week completed a debt refinancing\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  worth $6.6 billion in international markets, including\par a heavily over-subscribed bond offer.\par     The Brazilian real added 0.6% after the economy\par minister said Latin America's largest economy could surprise on\par the upside and grow more than 4% next year.    \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also said on Wednesday it will\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to curb year-end\par volatility caused by local banks unwinding their so-called\par overhedge positions.\par     "Although there are multiple factors pointing to a positive\par outlook for Brazil in the short to medium term\u8211\'20\'13including the\par stronger-than-expected recovery and preparations for mass\par vaccination, the fiscal outlook remains troubling," analysts at\par TS Lombard wrote in a note, adding that progress in fiscal\par reforms was a sticking point for the government's credibility. \par     The government had recently pledged to fast track reforms to\par privatization and fiscal spending.\par     Optimism about encouraging developments in vaccines for the\par novel coronavirus provided an initial boost to Latam risk\par assets, but like last week, the rally ran out of steam as \par infections continued to rise and more countries outlined\par economically-damaging lockdowns.\par     "(Vaccines)are unlikely to have much impact broadly until at\par least Q2. We think the market is a bit too sanguine and\par overlooking the near-term outlook, which looks to be more like a\par hole in the road than a speed bump," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mazen Issa\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  wrote in a note.\par     Chile's peso fell 0.1%, while Colombia's peso\par shed 0.2%.\par     Peru's sol was set to end a two-day winning streak as\par political uncertainty still weighed.\par     A gauge of Latin American stocks fell 0.4%\par after hitting a more-than eight-month high, while broader\par emerging market equities also retreated.\par     \par     Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par     \par                               Latest     Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets         1200.85              -0.55\par                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                    2182.01              -0.36\par                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa              106225.15                0.1\par                                         \par  Mexico IPC                   41995.30              -0.61\par                                         \par  Chile IPSA                    4028.50              -1.95\par                                         \par  Argentina MerVal             51243.13             -0.102\par                                         \par  Colombia COLCAP               1234.03              -0.04\par                                         \par                                                          \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              Latest     Daily % change\par  Brazil real                    5.3015               0.63\par                                         \par  Mexico peso                   20.1360               1.12\par                                         \par  Chile peso                      758.7              -0.11\par                                         \par  Colombia peso                 3647.95              -0.18\par  Peru sol                       3.5757              -0.17\par                                         \par  Argentina peso                80.2700              -0.12\par  (interbank)                            \par                                         \par   \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Shriya Ramakrishnan and Ambar Warrick in\par Bengaluru; editing by David Evans and Grant McCool)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-11-19T20:47:34.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201119egbj03q11\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
