\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ease as vaccine rally loses steam\b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2020\par 16:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Brazil GDP growth next year could top 4% - economy\par minister\par     * Mexico's peso set to snap a two-day losing streak \par     * Peru's sol on track to end a two-day winning streak\par \par     By Shriya Ramakrishnan\par     Nov 19 (Reuters) - Latin American stocks retreated from\par eight-month highs on Thursday and regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded in\par tight ranges, tracking a global pullback in equities as tighter\par coronavirus restrictions dented risk sentiment.\par     A gauge of Latin American stocks fell 1%\par after hitting its highest level since March 9 in the previous\par session, while its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  counterpart\par dropped 0.6%.\par     Optimism about encouraging vaccine developments provided an\par initial boost to risk assets in the region, but the rally ran\par out of steam as it did last week, after several countries\par announced record infection rates and tougher lockdowns.\par     While analysts have said the advent of a COVID-19 vaccine\par could spur inflows into riskier Latin American assets,\par short-term headwinds remain with regard to uncertainty over the\par availability and timeline of vaccine distribution.\par     The Brazilian real traded marginally lower, receiving\par some support after the country's economy minister said Latin\par America's largest economy could surprise on the upside and grow\par more than 4% next year.    \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday it will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if the market is unable to absorb\par the "large" outflow of reais expected by the end of the year as\par local banks unwind their so-called overhedge position.\par \par     "Although there are multiple factors pointing to a positive\par outlook for Brazil in the short to medium term\u8211\'20\'13including the\par stronger-than-expected recovery and preparations for mass\par vaccination, the fiscal outlook remains troubling," analysts at\par TS Lombard wrote in a note, adding that progress in fiscal\par reforms was a sticking point for the government's credibility. \par     Brazilian stocks traded 0.3% higher. \par     Mexico's peso strengthened 0.4% during the day and\par was set to snap a two-day losing streak. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has fared better than its Latam peers this year\par after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recently signaled a pause to\par its aggressive cycle of interest rate cuts, while Joe Biden's\par victory in the U.S. presidential election has also raised hopes\par for more stable trade policies.\par     Mexico earlier this week completed a debt refinancing\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  worth $6.6 billion in international markets, including\par a heavily over-subscribed bond offer.\par     Chile's peso edged down, tracking weakness in prices\par of copper, while Colombia's peso fell 0.2% as oil prices\par dipped after surging COVID-19 cases around the world raised\par worries over fuel demand.\par     Peru's sol was on track to end a two-day winning\par streak, after the appointment of Francisco Sagasti as the Andean\par nation's interim president restored some calm in markets. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :   \par     \par                                 Latest     Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets           1195.96              -0.96\par                                           \par  MSCI LatAm                      2167.64              -1.01\par                                           \par  Brazil Bovespa                106420.35               0.28\par                                           \par  Mexico IPC                            -                  -\par                                           \par  Chile IPSA                      4047.91              -1.48\par                                           \par  Argentina MerVal               51342.96              0.092\par                                           \par  Colombia COLCAP                 1234.93               0.03\par                                           \par                                                            \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2               Latest     Daily % change\par  Brazil real                      5.3382              -0.06\par                                           \par  Mexico peso                     20.2830               0.39\par                                           \par  Chile peso                        758.7              -0.11\par                                           \par  Colombia peso                   3649.68              -0.22\par  Peru sol                         3.5768              -0.20\par                                           \par  Argentina peso (interbank)      80.2600              -0.11\par                                           \par  \par \par  (Reporting by Shriya Ramakrishnan in Bengaluru; editing by\par David Evans)\f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-11-19T16:19:29.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201119egbj031su\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscal