\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  of  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  market if it detects imbalances at the end of the year\b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Nov 18 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the system is unable to absorb the huge output of expected reals by the end of the year, when it estimates that local banks will disarm their "over-cover" positions, the agency's monetary policy director Bruno Serra said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In comments for an online forum organized by the newspaper Valor Econ\u243\'00\'F3mico, Serra said that the total volume of brazilian banks' exposure was around $30 billion and that positions should be undone by half that amount as of December 31.\par \par \uc2 Recently, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility has declined, although it is still a little higher than \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities expect, he added. (Reports by Jamie McGeever and Isabel Versiani. Edited in Spanish by Marion Giraldo)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201118egbi006dz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
