\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank \highlight\uc2  says it does not flag upcoming  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  decisions\b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2020\par 23:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, quote)\par \par \uc2 By Jamie McGeever\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Nov 6 (Reuters) - \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday that it does not flag any decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in advance and rejects any suggestion it does, adding it constantly monitors financial markets to ensure they function smoothly.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement comes after economic policy director Fabio Kanczuk said on Friday that the bank could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease downward pressure on the real resulting from large year-end outflows related to banks' hedging activities.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterates that it continuously monitors the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and clarifies that it does not bring forward any decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "Decisions on the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions in the face of market dysfunction are made in a reasoned manner, in line with rigid internal governance procedures and guided by transparent communication through official channels," it said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Friday, Kanczuk gave a heavy hint that some form of dollar-selling or real-supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be carried out before the end of the year, as banks look to unwind so-called 'overhedge' trades put on to protect their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure on their overseas equity investments.\par \par \uc2 "The market needs to be big, big enough to withstand a very large (out)flow at the end of the year, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thinking about alternatives on how not to let this flow be disruptive," Kanczuk said.\par \par \uc2 "We are not sure the market will be able to absorb this, and think we will need to help," he added.\par \par \uc2 Traders said Kanczuk's comments helped lift the real to its highest level against the dollar in six weeks, and seal its biggest weekly rise since the first week of June.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold billions of dollars of its international reserves to stem heavy capital outflows this year. Last week, it sold $1.8 billion on the spot market.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 5.39 reais) (Reporting by Jamie McGeever; Editing by Leslie Adler and David Gregorio) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-11-6T23:52:06.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201106egb603qvl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
