\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexican peso up on data, Colombia's flat after hold on rates\b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2020\par 20:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Latam \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  index set for worst week in over one month\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Colombian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holds benchmark rate steady\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real rises after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par \par  (Updates prices throughout; adds bullets, comments)\par     By Shreyashi Sanyal\par     Oct 30 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso rose on Friday, set to end\par a tumultuous week on a positive note after data signaled a\par strong economic rebound, while the Colombian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded in\par a tight range after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept interest\par rates unchanged.     \par     The peso rose 0.7% against the dollar after\par preliminary data showed Mexico's economy grew 12.0% in the third\par quarter, making up for much of the contraction in the previous\par three months at the height of the coronavirus lockdown.\par \par     U.S. demand helped Mexico rack up large trade surpluses\par during the past four months, as exports picked up speed. By\par contrast, domestic demand has lagged, with many businesses still\par struggling.\par     A gauge for Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose\par 0.5%, gaining after three straight days of declines, but was\par still set for its worst weekly fall in over a month. \par     Most emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have come under pressure\par from a strengthening dollar in the face of rising coronavirus\par cases and uncertainty over the outcome of next week's U.S.\par presidential election. \par     Colombia's peso was flat after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left\par its benchmark interest rate unchanged at 1.75% as expected, the\par first hold after seven months of cuts that took borrowing costs\par to a historic low.     \par     Mexico's and Colombia's pesos have been pressured recently\par by a slide in oil prices. \par     The Brazilian real rose 0.3%, after the\par country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par on Friday, selling dollars to ease heavy downward pressure on\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that had pushed it closer to its all-time low\par against the dollar struck earlier this year.\par     Brazil's real shed 2.2% this week, the most among its Latin\par American peers on general risk aversion and worries about the\par countries public finances. \par     "There are idiosyncratic factors that make BRL more\par susceptible than other EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," wrote You-Na Park-Heger\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and emerging market analyst at Commerzbank.  \par     "First of all, there is the high budget deficit and the lack\par of progress with the fiscal reforms. And secondly the\par historically low key rates are also putting pressure on BRL."\par     The Chilean peso was flat against the dollar. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chile's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unanimously opted to keep interest rates at a\par baseline low this month, agreeing that while the worst of the\par COVID-19 pandemic was "now behind us" there were fresh risks in\par the medium term, according to minutes released on Friday.\par \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1900 GMT:\par     \par           Stock indexes                   Latest   Daily %\par                                                    change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets                    1102.12    -1.61\par  MSCI LatAm                               1808.01    -1.37\par  Brazil Bovespa                          94028.08    -2.64\par  Mexico IPC                              36866.06     0.18\par  Chile IPSA                               3549.27    -0.93\par  Argentina MerVal                        44988.08    0.164\par  Colombia COLCAP                          1146.00      1.3\par                                                           \par               \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                   Latest   Daily %\par                                                    change\par  Brazil real                               5.7462     0.29\par  Mexico peso                              21.2480     0.65\par  Chile peso                                 773.5    -0.12\par  Colombia peso                            3868.85    -0.24\par  Peru sol                                  3.6148    -0.11\par  Argentina peso (interbank)               78.3200    -0.03\par                                                    \par  Argentina peso (parallel)                    165     6.06\par                                                    \par  \par  (Reporting by Shreyashi Sanyal in Bengaluru; editing by Emelia\par Sithole-Matarise and Tom Brown)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-10-30T20:26:56.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201030egau042lt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
