\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank \highlight \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  as real slumps across the board\b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2020\par 17:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Oct 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, selling dollars to ease heavy downward pressure on the real that had pushed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closer to its all-time low against the dollar struck earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $787 million in the spot market as the greenback topped 5.80 reais for the first time since May, closing in on its all-time high just under 6.00 reais that month.\par \par \uc2 This follows the sale of $1 billion in the spot market on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Investor concerns over the fiscal outlook, coupled with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's pledge to keep official interest rates anchored at their record low for some time to come, have weighed heavily on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and steepened the rates curve this week.\par \par \uc2 "Monetary policy is overloading the (rates) curve and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On top of that there's no (fiscal) plan and agenda," said a senior trader at a bank in Sao Paulo. "It's that simple."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action drove the real to 5.76 per dollar from above 5.81. Having slumped to a record low against sterling of 7.51 per pound, the real recovered a bit to 7.46 per pound. \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real is one of the worst-performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year, having lost more than 30% of its value against the dollar since January.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Figures on Friday showed the national debt rising to a record high above 90% of gross domestic product in September, and unemployment rising to an all-time high of 14.4% in the three months to August. .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier this week the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept its Selic interest rate on hold at a record low 2.00%, and surprised some analysts by maintaining its 'forward guidance' pledge to keep it low for longer, despite the growing fiscal fears.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Jamie McGeever; Editing by Steve Orlofsky) \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-10-30T17:06:32.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201030egau03i06\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
