\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  drops as Brazil's real underperforms for the week\b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2020\par 21:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Brazil's real to lose more than 3% this week\par     * Chile's peso to outperform regional peers for the week\par     * Commodity-sensitive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weaken\par \par  (Adds details, updates prices)\par     By Susan Mathew and Ambar Warrick\par     Aug 21 (Reuters) - Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell on Friday\par amid signs of a stalling global economic recovery from the\par coronavirus, with Brazil's real set to underperform for the week\par on uncertainty over the country's fiscal position. \par     The real fell around 1%, staying near three-month\par lows, and was set to lose more than 3% for the week. The\par country's lower house of Congress on Thursday voted to uphold a\par presidential veto blocking pay increases for civil servants.\par     Speculation over the vote had increased concerns over\par Brazil's already stretched fiscal position, which has come under\par pressure from higher spending due to the coronavirus.\par \par     The move "shows that the resistance to implement an austere\par fiscal (policy) is bigger than previously expected," said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategists at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2 , adding they expect fiscal discussions\par to remain in the spotlight as the government is to deliver the\par 2021 budget law by the end of August.\par     "We anticipate (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue\par softening moves with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in swaps and spot if the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bleeds heavily."   \par     Stocks in Sao Paulo fell, led by financials and\par materials.\par     Still, the country marked its strongest July job growth for\par eight years, snapping four consecutive months of job losses as\par it continued to relax virus-related restrictions on business\par activity.\par     Most Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under pressure after the\par dollar surged on disappointing business activity data from\par Europe. A cautious stance from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  earlier\par in the week had hurt risk appetite.\par     An unabated rise in COVID-19 cases also weighed. The number\par of reported COVID-19 deaths in Latin America passed 250,000 on\par Thursday, as the virus afflicts the region, which has become the\par worst hit in the world.\par     Sliding oil prices dragged crude exporter Colombia's peso\par , while Chile's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was undercut by a drop in\par copper prices.\par     Optimism over recovering demand for copper had helped\par Chile's peso, putting it on course to outperform its regional\par peers this week.\par     Mexico's peso rose slightly after data showed some\par improvement in retail sales in the country, signaling that a\par recovery from the pandemic was under way.\par     Mexican stocks, however, sank more than 1%. The\par MSCI's index of Latin American stocks was set to\par lose more than 3% for the week.\par     Argentine stocks rose slightly amid further signs of\par progress in the country's restructuring of its sovereign debt.\par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\par     \par     Stock indexes             Latest      Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets         1090.82                 0.95\par                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                    1947.44                -0.01\par                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa              101067.51                -0.39\par                                         \par  Mexico IPC                   38238.97                -1.21\par                                         \par  Chile IPSA                    3980.81                 0.07\par                                         \par  Argentina MerVal             48049.85                0.655\par                                         \par  Colombia COLCAP               1183.88                 0.83\par                                         \par                                                            \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              Latest      Daily % change\par  Brazil real                    5.6090                -1.01\par                                         \par  Mexico peso                   21.9600                 0.52\par                                         \par  Chile peso                      791.9                -0.73\par                                         \par  Colombia peso                 3833.25                -0.80\par  Peru sol                       3.5827                -0.16\par                                         \par  Argentina peso                73.5700                -0.05\par  (interbank)                            \par                                         \par  \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew in Bengaluru; Editing by Nick\par Macfie)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-8-21T20:24:19.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200821eg8l036nt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
