\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real jumps on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  reassurance\b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2020\par 22:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ready to increase \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par chief\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of oil-exporters Mexico, Colombia rise\par     * Argentina creditor says default hard to avoid on Friday \par \par  (Adds comments, updates prices)\par     By Shreyashi Sanyal and Susan Mathew\par     May 21 (Reuters) - Brazil's real jumped on Thursday after\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it remained ready to increase support for\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Mexico's peso hit its highest in nearly two\par months as oil prices rallied.\par     But as the novel coronavirus speeds through the region,\par analysts said the Latin American economy may shrink at a record\par pace this year and take at least two more years to recover.\par    \par     Brazil is seen soon becoming the second-worst hit globally\par as the number of cases approaches 300,000, while Mexico reported\par a surge in cases after reopening its economy. \par  \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Mexico and Colombia both rose\par around 1.3% as recovering demand lifted oil prices.\par \par     Brazil's real jumped 2% after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Roberto Campos Neto\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the bank would dip into its large pool\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves and continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if needed. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost close to 30% of\par its value against the dollar so far this year.\par     Amid increasing political uncertainty in Brazil, the\par government's remaining 'super minister,' Economy Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paulo\par Guedes\f28 \uc2 \f2 , has the full support of his team, a senior ministry\par official said on Wednesday.\par     Mexican President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Andres Manuel Lopez Obrador\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the\par government was open to dialogue about rule changes in the\par electricity sector that had sent the stock market plunging.\par Mexico's \f28 \uc2 \f2 IPC\f28 \uc2 \f2  index fell 1%. \par     Most Latam bourses rose with Brazil's benchmark index\par  hitting a three-week high.\par     "We think Latin America offers the most value in EM equities\par \u8211\'20\'13 Bovespa likely the best rebound candidate," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par strategists in a note.\par     "Latin America's underperformance versus the rest of EM\par since January has opened up significant value across assets on\par both a relative and an absolute basis," they said, also\par highlighting tail-winds from an expected pick-up in commodity\par prices in the second half of 2020.\par     Argentina's peso slid deeper into record low\par territory as the government probably cannot avoid defaulting on\par a bond payment due on Friday. But one of its creditors, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Greylock\par Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said a deal to restructure $65 billion in foreign debt\par should still be achievable.\par                 \par     Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1946 GMT:\par     \par       Stock indexes               Latest       Daily %\par                                                change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets               929.82        -0.18\par                                              \par  MSCI LatAm                         1675.76         2.32\par                                              \par  Brazil Bovespa                    83067.44         2.15\par  Mexico IPC                        35650.45        -1.05\par  Chile IPSA                         3755.08         0.67\par                                              \par  Argentina MerVal                  41389.04        3.969\par                                              \par  Colombia COLCAP                    1068.45        -0.36\par                                              \par                                                         \par          \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest       Daily %\par                                                change\par  Brazil real                         5.5776         1.99\par                                              \par  Mexico peso                        22.9010         1.27\par                                              \par  Chile peso                           802.7         0.00\par                                              \par  Colombia peso                      3759.97         1.21\par  Peru sol                            3.4108        -0.30\par                                              \par  Argentina peso (interbank)         68.0800        -0.12\par                                              \par  \par  (Reporting by Shreyashi Sanyal and Susan Mathew in Bengaluru;\par Editing by Andrea Ricci and Grant McCool)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-5-21T21:00:30.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200521eg5l02ysh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
