\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  ready to increase  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  but cautious on bond buying - \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  chief\b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2020\par 01:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 By Jamie McGeever and Marcela Ayres\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, May 20 (Reuters) - Brazil stands ready to dip into its large pool of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed, but any bond market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to be far smaller in size, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Roberto Campos Neto\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real has lost around 30% of its value and is one of the worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar this year. A combination of record low interest rates, a sharply deteriorating economy because of the coronavirus pandemic and political uncertainty has pulled capital out of the country.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at an online event hosted by infrastructure and industry umbrella group Abdib, \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said the scale of capital outflows in March was surprising, and that the bank increased its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it was apparent the real was decoupling from other emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Brazil has a lot of reserves, and as a percentage of GDP they have actually risen because the (\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) depreciation has been greater than the amount we have sold," \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "There is a lot of room to sell reserves. We will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and may even increase that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if we believe it is necessary."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves fell $23 billion in March as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  upped its dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter a record portfolio outflow of almost the exact same amount. Total reserves at the end of April were about $320 billion, the lowest since 2011.\par \par \uc2 On bond-buying, however, \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said he preferred targeted action to provide liquidity and manage the interest rate curve when markets seize up.\par \par \uc2 "We don't think we should do anything more than that until we're sure the power of monetary policy has run out," he said.\par \par \uc2 The bank has emergency powers to buy sovereign bonds on the secondary market, but the 'quantitative easing' asset purchases in many developed economies appear unlikely. (Reporting by Jamie McGeever and Marcela Ayres Editing by Chris Reese) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-5-21T00:45:11.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200520eg5k03led\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
