\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Brazil real sinks to new low on rate cut, 6.00 per dollar in sight\b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2020\par 22:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quote)               \par \par \uc2 By Jamie McGeever               \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, May 7 (Reuters) - Brazil's real sank to a new all-time low against the dollar on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surprisingly large interest rate cut, bringing a test of the previously unthinkable 6.00 level within view.               \par \par \uc2 The fall brings the real's decline against the dollar this year to 31%, cementing its status as one of the worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the greenback so far this year, and puts it on course for its biggest weekly decline in nearly five years.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed its benchmark Selic rate by 75 basis points to a record-low 3.00% on Wednesday and indicated it could repeat the dose next month, as it battles the deepening economic crisis fueled by the coronavirus pandemic.               \par \par \uc2 Analysts expressed surprise that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement made no reference to the exchange rate, given the real's steep decline this year. The forward guidance of another chunky rate cut, even though it might be the last in the cycle, intensified the selling pressure on Thursday, they added.               \par \par \uc2 "The market reacted as you would expect: real falling, curve steepening. There were no (dollar) sellers today other than speculators and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Cleber Alessie Machado, broker at Commcor DTVM in Sao Paulo.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling dollar swaps contracts, which relieved some of the pressure and prevented a test of 5.90 per dollar. But analysts say that is only a matter of time, then the big one.               \par \par \uc2 "The real is likely to breach the 6.00 figure soon, and I wouldn't bet against it going even higher," said a senior trader in Sao Paulo.                                             \par \par \uc2 The real traded as low as 5.8760 per dollar on Thursday, down more than 2% on the day and bringing its losses for the week so far to 6%. A decline of around 0.5% on Friday will seal its biggest weekly fall since September 2015.               \par \par \uc2 Economy Ministry officials, including minister \uc2 Paulo Guedes\uc2 , have repeatedly said they are comfortable with a monetary policy mix of low interest rates and a weak exchange rate, the opposite of what \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  had experienced for many years.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling dollars several times this year, but policymakers have made it clear they are not doing so to set a level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 Interest rate spreads widened on Thursday, reflecting the prospect of more policy easing but growing risks of capital outflows, market volatility and deteriorating investor sentiment stemming from the weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 The January 2021-January 2029 interest rate futures spread widened nearly 50 basis points to 570 basis points .                                             \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-5-7T21:37:36.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200507eg5702h1l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
