\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real tumbles; Broader Latam slightly helped by stimulus cheer\b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2020\par 16:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par     * MSCI Latam stocks index rises 3%\par     * Mexican, Colombian pesos lead gains in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par \par     By Ambar Warrick\par     April 27 (Reuters) - Brazil's real eyed a fresh record low\par on Monday after plummeting last week, while Mexico's peso led\par other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher as continued global\par stimulus measures sparked some appetite for riskier assets. \par     The real fell about 0.9%. Its sharp decline since the\par coronavirus outbreak, which has seen it underperforming its\par peers, has prompted sustained \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazilian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stop further weakness.\par     The resignation of Brazil's popular justice minister last\par week dealt a severe blow to Brazilian President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jair Bolsonaro\f28 \uc2 \f2 ,\par who had already faced backlash over his handling of the\par coronavirus outbreak.\par     Investors further cut their exposure to Brazil on the\par likelihood Latin America's largest economy was headed for a\par political crisis. \par     The Mexican peso and the Colombian peso edged\par up for the day, taking some support from increased stimulus\par measures in Japan to dampen the economic shock from the\par coronavirus pandemic, which has battered the global economy.\par     Still, both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were relatively close to lifetime\par lows hit during the initial rout caused by the spread of the\par virus, which has spurred sustained outflows from emerging\par markets in favor of the U.S. dollar. \par     The pandemic is also expected to hit emerging markets\par particularly hard, given that many economies in that space were\par already in dire straits before the outbreak culled business\par activity across the globe.\par     "We see risks skewed towards a renewed increase in EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par volatility as the economic shock on EM economies intensifies and\par risks of further waves of virus cases increases," wrote Mitul\par Kotecha, senior emerging markets strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "Unlike developed economies, the capacity for EM governments\par and central banks to deal with the economic and health shock is\par lower." \par     However, Latin American stocks have been slightly more\par receptive to the slight improvement in risk appetite, with the\par MSCI's index of regional stocks adding 3% for\par the day.\par     The index is nearly 10% above the lows hit in March, but is\par a long way off levels seen prior to the outbreak.\par     Brazilian stocks added 3.6%, recovering from deep\par losses over last week, while Chilean stocks rose 1.2%.\par     Among notable individual movers, shares of Brazilian\par planemaker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Embraer SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  plunged 12% after it began\par arbitration proceedings against former partner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boeing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par \par     Markets were now awaiting the outcomes of crucial \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meetings in the developed world to gauge further how the\par world's largest economies outline measures to combat the\par coronavirus pandemic.\par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1405 GMT\par     \par     Stock indexes             Latest      Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets          895.38                 1.82\par                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                    1547.19                    3\par                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa               78067.88                 3.63\par                                         \par  Mexico IPC                   34538.55                -0.14\par                                         \par  Chile IPSA                    3723.91                  1.2\par                                         \par  Argentina MerVal                    -                    -\par                                         \par  Colombia COLCAP               1115.98                -0.57\par                                         \par                                                            \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              Latest      Daily % change\par  Brazil real                    5.6344                -0.91\par                                         \par  Mexico peso                   24.7950                 0.62\par                                         \par  Chile peso                      857.2                 0.19\par                                         \par  Colombia peso                 4025.87                 0.33\par  Peru sol                       3.3897                 0.15\par                                         \par  Argentina peso                66.5200                -0.14\par  (interbank)                            \par                                         \par  \par \par  (Reporting by Ambar Warrick in Bengaluru\par Editing by Paul Simao)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-4-27T15:27:43.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokume