\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam assets pause two-day rally as coronavirus concerns persist\b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2020\par 16:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ambar Warrick\par     April 8 (Reuters) - Brazil's real dipped on Wednesday, while\par most other Latin American stocks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  treaded water as\par a two-day rally was stymied by continued concerns over the\par coronavirus outbreak.\par     The virus' death toll and spread continued to increase,\par while its economic impact loomed over markets as more countries\par impose lockdowns in a bid to stem its spread.\par     Emerging market risk assets were hit particularly hard by\par the drop in risk appetite, with the MSCI's Latin American stocks\par  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  indexes now\par trading just above multiyear lows.\par     For the day, the two indexes were flat.\par     "The stock market rallies of the past two days are despite\par the fact that neither economic nor earnings data have really\par begun to unveil the enormity of the economic crisis that the\par world has been plunging into in the past few weeks," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par analysts wrote in a note.\par     Anticipation ahead of a key OPEC+ meeting on Thursday, which\par is expected to result in major oil producers cutting production,\par also kept markets on their toes. The minutes of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's meeting last month were also awaited.\par     "Today\u8217\'20\'19s release of the minutes of the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s March meetings\par can be expected to display how panicked policy makers were last\par month. This should be another sobering reminder of the enormity\par of the current crisis,"  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts said.\par      The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Mexico and Colombia, both\par major oil exporters, inched higher on the prospect of a recovery\par in oil prices.\par     Brazilian stocks rose about 0.2%, taking some\par support from a stronger open on Wall Street.\par     Oil and gas heavyweight \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2  was the biggest\par boost to the Bovespa, adding more than 2.5% after it outlined\par further cost cuts. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Roberto Campos Neto\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the president of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par pledged aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to\par prop up the real, which has lost nearly a third of its value\par over the last quarter.\par     The real fell 0.4% on Wednesday.\par     Chile's peso rose 1%, while stocks in the country\par  traded sideways. Inflation in the 12 months to March\par rose 3.7% in the country, but was within the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par target range.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1502 GMT\par     \par     Stock indexes             Latest      Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets          872.21                -0.68\par                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                    1621.79                 0.14\par                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa               76718.75                 0.47\par                                         \par  Mexico IPC                   34604.91                 0.23\par                                         \par  Chile IPSA                    3723.35                 0.31\par      