\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank \highlight\uc2  focusing on bank liquidity, says  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  a success\b0\par\par\uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 18:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Jamie McGeever and Marcela Ayres\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, March 26 (Reuters) - \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely monitoring financial markets and will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to provide liquidity where it sees fit, although this will not include buying companies' debt, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president \uc2 Roberto Campos Neto\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The main channel of support for the financial system remains ensuring banks have ample liquidity, \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to inject liquidity and ease stress in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market have been successful.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in an online virtual press conference after the bank slashed its 2020 economic growth forecast to zero due to the impact of the coronavirus, \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  also said the bank was working toward bringing inflation up toward target.\par \par \uc2 "It was important to act to provide stability and liquidity (to banks)," \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said, noting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent measures to offer financing to banks in return for debentures collateral, and issue notes to banks backed by securitized loans.\par \par \uc2 "We don't have the tools to buy debt directly, so we are putting together a package of measures to address the potential dysfunction in credit markets that could arise. But so far markets have functioned smoothly," he said.\par \par \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is relaxed about the financial system, although it continues to monitor it closely and has increased the frequency with which it carries out bank stress tests.\par \par \uc2 He reiterated that the bank has a wide range of tools at its disposal to tackle market disruption amid the current crisis, and said its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a success and that it continues to monitor the market closely.\par \par \uc2 On inflation, \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said that all the bank's forecasts using various interest and exchange rate assumptions show inflation below target, potentially as low as 2.6% this year and 3.2% next.\par \par \uc2 But economic policy director Fabio Kanczuk said the bank's 50 basis point interest rate cut last week remained appropriate, even in light of the rapid deterioration in the economic outlook since then.\par \par \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said policymakers discussed a wide range of potential scenarios surrounding the coronavirus shock but added that a more aggressive rate cut could have tightened financial conditions.\par \par \uc2 The hit to demand will have a greater bearing on inflation than the supply shock, Kanczuk said, a sign that the bank might cut rates again soon. (Reporting by Jamie McGeever and Marcela Ayres; Editing by Steve Orlofsky) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-3-26T18:25:48.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200326eg3q03wg0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
